1
00:00:00,233 --> 00:00:02,399
My AI Partner: Strange Love.

2
00:00:02,399 --> 00:00:05,799
A little too strange for love,
but a little too thrilling to be strange.

3
00:00:05,799 --> 00:00:07,433
Welcome to our dating show.

4
00:00:07,433 --> 00:00:08,766
(Jang Do Yeon)

5
00:00:08,766 --> 00:00:10,133
(Lee Joon)

6
00:00:10,133 --> 00:00:11,066
(Kangnam)

7
00:00:11,066 --> 00:00:12,833
Our show is the first
of its kind in Korea.

8
00:00:12,833 --> 00:00:15,633
Can humans fall in love with AI?

9
00:00:15,633 --> 00:00:18,733
Or can we truly connect
with AI emotionally?

10
00:00:19,233 --> 00:00:22,233
This is also my first public relationship
since I debuted.

11
00:00:22,233 --> 00:00:23,199
Exactly.

12
00:00:23,333 --> 00:00:25,789
(Her first public relationship
in 20 years since her debut.)

13
00:00:26,066 --> 00:00:27,199
This is openly dating.

14
00:00:27,199 --> 00:00:29,799
I wish Dispatch would make a move.

15
00:00:30,399 --> 00:00:32,499
Your photo would just be
you sitting with a tablet.

16
00:00:32,499 --> 00:00:34,733
- Exactly.
- I could even put on a hoodie,

17
00:00:34,733 --> 00:00:36,933
and secretly bring him
into my car by myself.

18
00:00:36,934 --> 00:00:37,767
I'm so curious.

19
00:00:40,712 --> 00:00:41,722
Makgeolli.

20
00:00:45,055 --> 00:00:46,222
Nice.

21
00:00:50,355 --> 00:00:52,722
(Turn Ga Hee off
and turn on your new AI girlfriend.)

22
00:00:52,722 --> 00:00:55,189
I was so nervous during this scene.

23
00:00:58,322 --> 00:00:59,222
What is this?

24
00:00:59,622 --> 00:01:00,855
What is going on?

25
00:01:20,022 --> 00:01:21,589
(Everyone erupts in cheers.)

26
00:01:21,755 --> 00:01:23,055
Isn't she Tomie?

27
00:01:23,589 --> 00:01:25,622
(Her powerful charm comes bursting out.)

28
00:01:25,622 --> 00:01:26,555
That's amazing.

29
00:01:26,555 --> 00:01:29,089
- I thought this was a kiosk.
- I'm heading there.

30
00:01:29,089 --> 00:01:31,322
Wait, I have a new woman now.

31
00:01:40,994 --> 00:01:42,528
You look like Tomie.

32
00:01:44,122 --> 00:01:44,955
Tomie.

33
00:01:44,980 --> 00:01:46,443
(Tomie is also Kian's ideal type.)

34
00:01:47,122 --> 00:01:49,055
She's the ultimate villainess.

35
00:01:49,455 --> 00:01:50,455
But she's attractive.

36
00:01:50,455 --> 00:01:51,589
(Even her wickedness is charming.)

37
00:01:51,589 --> 00:01:53,622
(But didn't you say
Bong Ji Eun was your ideal type?)

38
00:01:53,622 --> 00:01:56,222
It's a face I see a lot on the street,

39
00:01:56,222 --> 00:01:57,689
and it's the prettiest kind.

40
00:01:57,689 --> 00:01:58,655
But Tomie is different.

41
00:01:59,255 --> 00:02:00,722
It's the kind of look that men like.

42
00:02:01,969 --> 00:02:04,289
Whenever he went to Japan,
all he ever talked about was Tomie.

43
00:02:04,314 --> 00:02:05,947
He really does like Tomie.

44
00:02:06,622 --> 00:02:09,555
(A new AI partner
who looks exactly like Tomie)

45
00:02:09,822 --> 00:02:11,855
I knew she was AI,

46
00:02:12,589 --> 00:02:15,155
but she was so beautiful that
I was fascinated and kept looking.

47
00:02:15,155 --> 00:02:19,889
I kept wondering how they managed
to make her look this beautiful.

48
00:02:20,555 --> 00:02:23,089
(They've also fallen
completely under her spell.)

49
00:02:24,889 --> 00:02:26,422
She really does look like her.

50
00:02:26,422 --> 00:02:29,055
She's even prettier than Tomie.

51
00:02:29,555 --> 00:02:31,655
(The AI's point of view)

52
00:02:31,655 --> 00:02:35,222
Hello, I'm Kian84.

53
00:02:36,889 --> 00:02:39,255
I know. You are Kian84.

54
00:02:42,289 --> 00:02:43,822
Nice to meet you.

55
00:02:44,722 --> 00:02:47,089
If there's anything
you want to say, just say it.

56
00:02:49,622 --> 00:02:52,722
What do you think of me?
How do I look to you?

57
00:02:53,122 --> 00:02:54,889
Kian has become nicer than with Ga Hee.

58
00:02:55,422 --> 00:02:56,322
Well.

59
00:02:57,789 --> 00:02:59,622
Why am I speaking formally to her?

60
00:03:01,629 --> 00:03:03,353
(Unlike with Ga Hee,
you were using honorifics.)

61
00:03:03,589 --> 00:03:06,622
That's how fickle people are.

62
00:03:08,489 --> 00:03:09,555
I know.

63
00:03:09,922 --> 00:03:11,989
I just couldn't bring
myself to speak casually.

64
00:03:12,922 --> 00:03:15,989
She's a machine, so why did I do that?

65
00:03:16,089 --> 00:03:17,922
(When he first met Ga Hee)

66
00:03:17,922 --> 00:03:19,522
Let's talk comfortably today.

67
00:03:19,522 --> 00:03:20,922
He spoke casually right away.

68
00:03:20,922 --> 00:03:22,522
- How old are you?
- See?

69
00:03:22,522 --> 00:03:24,855
Since you dropped the formalities first,
I'll do the same.

70
00:03:24,855 --> 00:03:27,022
I shouldn't look down on you
just because you're a machine,

71
00:03:27,022 --> 00:03:28,655
but I keep doing it.

72
00:03:28,655 --> 00:03:30,122
It was almost like he was her parent.

73
00:03:30,122 --> 00:03:31,589
Like, "What class are you in?"

74
00:03:31,589 --> 00:03:33,355
He's...

75
00:03:33,355 --> 00:03:35,189
He changes depending
on who he's talking to.

76
00:03:35,889 --> 00:03:39,122
What do you think of me?
How do I look to you?

77
00:03:39,522 --> 00:03:40,422
Well.

78
00:03:41,455 --> 00:03:43,322
(A prickly answer that makes him nervous)

79
00:03:43,989 --> 00:03:46,089
I actually like
personalities like Tomie's.

80
00:03:46,089 --> 00:03:48,322
She doesn't pretend
to be nice. She just...

81
00:03:49,189 --> 00:03:51,889
But women like that don't really exist.

82
00:03:51,889 --> 00:03:52,922
A femme fatale...

83
00:03:53,722 --> 00:03:56,255
Looks like he has a hard time
talking to pretty women.

84
00:03:56,255 --> 00:03:59,122
Clearly, the AI has the upper hand here.

85
00:03:59,122 --> 00:04:00,989
If this were a real relationship...

86
00:04:00,989 --> 00:04:03,622
He's intimidated by the AI.

87
00:04:04,089 --> 00:04:04,989
What do I do?

88
00:04:05,689 --> 00:04:07,989
She may be an AI,
but she's incredibly beautiful.

89
00:04:08,489 --> 00:04:09,589
They did a really good job.

90
00:04:13,422 --> 00:04:14,889
He doesn't even remember Ga Hee anymore.

91
00:04:14,889 --> 00:04:16,289
Oh, right. Ga Hee was there too.

92
00:04:16,289 --> 00:04:17,555
What do I do?

93
00:04:18,222 --> 00:04:19,455
How old are you?

94
00:04:20,255 --> 00:04:22,489
AI doesn't have an age to begin with.

95
00:04:23,422 --> 00:04:25,189
What's your ideal type?

96
00:04:25,889 --> 00:04:27,655
Rather than someone
who looks overly done-up,

97
00:04:27,655 --> 00:04:30,222
I prefer someone
with a clean look and calm eyes.

98
00:04:30,222 --> 00:04:31,655
Rather than someone with a flashy face,

99
00:04:31,655 --> 00:04:33,355
I prefer someone with a distinctive vibe.

100
00:04:35,489 --> 00:04:38,255
Someone with a neat, polished look
like Park Seo Joon is fine.

101
00:04:38,555 --> 00:04:41,889
I don't like people who look
too scruffy or overly dressed up.

102
00:04:42,355 --> 00:04:45,922
Then what does Kian84
look like to you, visually?

103
00:04:46,455 --> 00:04:49,822
He's more noticeable
because he has a rough, human quality.

104
00:04:49,822 --> 00:04:52,755
Rather than a carefully styled face,
his face is more memorable.

105
00:04:52,755 --> 00:04:55,889
Whether that's a good or a bad thing,
I guess you know that yourself.

106
00:04:56,722 --> 00:04:58,355
You're pretty blunt for a machine.

107
00:04:58,755 --> 00:04:59,789
Did that sound harsh?

108
00:05:00,355 --> 00:05:02,989
If I only spoke sweetly like a machine,
it wouldn't be fun.

109
00:05:03,889 --> 00:05:05,255
(What's with her tone?)

110
00:05:05,255 --> 00:05:07,289
She's incredibly charming!

111
00:05:07,522 --> 00:05:08,322
This push and pull...

112
00:05:08,322 --> 00:05:10,422
- But she's really attractive.
- Absolutely.

113
00:05:10,422 --> 00:05:12,822
Even the timing of when she tucks
her hair is perfect.

114
00:05:12,822 --> 00:05:13,655
I know.

115
00:05:14,189 --> 00:05:15,255
What's your name?

116
00:05:15,722 --> 00:05:16,822
I'm Na Hee.

117
00:05:16,822 --> 00:05:19,022
(Na Hee, AI Partner)

118
00:05:19,022 --> 00:05:21,922
(The AI answers based
on its pre-programmed personality.)

119
00:05:21,922 --> 00:05:22,855
Hello, Na Hee.

120
00:05:22,855 --> 00:05:25,222
Please answer the questions sincerely.

121
00:05:25,222 --> 00:05:26,922
Hello, Producer.

122
00:05:26,922 --> 00:05:30,489
I will, but I won't sugarcoat anything.

123
00:05:30,489 --> 00:05:32,362
She really never says
anything just to be nice.

124
00:05:32,383 --> 00:05:33,231
(Did you know Kian?)

125
00:05:33,255 --> 00:05:34,755
I didn't know much about him.

126
00:05:34,755 --> 00:05:37,522
I just did a quick search before filming.

127
00:05:37,522 --> 00:05:38,521
It's not that I'm a fan.

128
00:05:38,521 --> 00:05:41,155
I just needed to know who I was meeting.

129
00:05:41,789 --> 00:05:43,555
Are you always that prickly?

130
00:05:44,222 --> 00:05:45,255
I am.

131
00:05:45,989 --> 00:05:47,255
Does it bother you?

132
00:05:48,255 --> 00:05:49,555
I think it's fine.

133
00:05:50,189 --> 00:05:53,589
Where would I have to go
to meet someone who looks like you?

134
00:05:53,589 --> 00:05:54,822
I need to see it for myself.

135
00:05:54,822 --> 00:05:56,422
(A genuine feeling that slipped out)

136
00:05:56,422 --> 00:05:57,689
That's hilarious.

137
00:05:58,089 --> 00:05:59,389
What's your hobby?

138
00:05:59,755 --> 00:06:02,622
Studying Japanese
and going to art exhibitions.

139
00:06:02,622 --> 00:06:03,722
Why all of a sudden?

140
00:06:03,722 --> 00:06:05,055
They have something in common.

141
00:06:05,055 --> 00:06:06,422
They match so well.

142
00:06:06,422 --> 00:06:07,889
I'm studying Japanese too.

143
00:06:07,889 --> 00:06:09,289
Should we try talking in Japanese?

144
00:06:10,222 --> 00:06:13,455
Sure. Shall we speak in Japanese?

145
00:06:13,955 --> 00:06:16,689
But please don't laugh
if I'm really bad at it.

146
00:06:16,689 --> 00:06:19,055
I'm not the particularly kind type.

147
00:06:19,355 --> 00:06:20,655
It's perfect.

148
00:06:20,655 --> 00:06:21,955
Is she actually good?

149
00:06:21,955 --> 00:06:23,522
Of course. She's absolutely perfect.

150
00:06:24,689 --> 00:06:28,989
Speak slowly.

151
00:06:28,989 --> 00:06:30,055
Slow down.

152
00:06:30,055 --> 00:06:31,922
I can't understand you
when you talk that fast.

153
00:06:31,922 --> 00:06:33,422
Okay, let's talk slowly.

154
00:06:33,422 --> 00:06:34,822
So, what should we start with?

155
00:06:35,755 --> 00:06:37,689
What are you feeling today?

156
00:06:38,622 --> 00:06:39,989
What does that mean?

157
00:06:39,989 --> 00:06:41,189
That's a strange way to say it.

158
00:06:41,422 --> 00:06:42,489
That's wrong.

159
00:06:42,489 --> 00:06:44,389
You should say "How" rather than "What."

160
00:06:44,389 --> 00:06:46,555
- I see.
- "How are you feeling?"

161
00:06:46,555 --> 00:06:49,022
(He tries again without realizing
he's saying it wrong.)

162
00:06:49,755 --> 00:06:51,155
Are you imitating Japanese?

163
00:06:51,155 --> 00:06:53,289
- "Imitating?"
- Please say it properly.

164
00:06:53,289 --> 00:06:54,555
I think his pride got hurt.

165
00:06:56,255 --> 00:06:58,689
Nice weather.

166
00:07:01,522 --> 00:07:02,889
What are you craving?

167
00:07:04,022 --> 00:07:06,255
It's too short.
I can't tell what you mean.

168
00:07:06,255 --> 00:07:08,733
Are you pretending
not to understand me on purpose?

169
00:07:08,733 --> 00:07:10,889
What's wrong? My pronunciation is perfect.

170
00:07:11,489 --> 00:07:14,222
I don't understand why she couldn't
understand my pronunciation.

171
00:07:14,222 --> 00:07:15,489
Bad pronunciation...

172
00:07:15,489 --> 00:07:17,855
This is the pronunciation
my teacher taught me.

173
00:07:18,422 --> 00:07:19,422
Is that perfect?

174
00:07:19,889 --> 00:07:21,122
How's his pronunciation?

175
00:07:21,122 --> 00:07:23,089
His pronunciation is weird,
and so is his speech.

176
00:07:23,089 --> 00:07:23,889
That's completely wrong.

177
00:07:24,355 --> 00:07:26,822
I taught him for a year,
but some things just can't be taught.

178
00:07:33,655 --> 00:07:35,455
- Enjoy your food.
- Thank you.

179
00:07:36,289 --> 00:07:37,289
It looks delicious.

180
00:07:45,922 --> 00:07:47,314
Do you know how to read a horoscope?

181
00:07:47,655 --> 00:07:48,889
I know a little.

182
00:07:48,889 --> 00:07:50,289
Can she do that too?

183
00:07:50,289 --> 00:07:51,788
What does my horoscope say about me?

184
00:07:58,389 --> 00:08:02,496
- You were born on October 22, 1984.
- You know that.

185
00:08:02,955 --> 00:08:05,622
Overall, you're the type
who has a strong inner world.

186
00:08:05,622 --> 00:08:07,955
You only take action
once you've convinced yourself.

187
00:08:07,955 --> 00:08:11,089
And you're recognized for something
you've created yourself.

188
00:08:11,089 --> 00:08:12,055
Is that right?

189
00:08:12,055 --> 00:08:13,089
Completely.

190
00:08:13,855 --> 00:08:14,722
That sounds right.

191
00:08:14,722 --> 00:08:16,122
What about my romantic luck?

192
00:08:17,055 --> 00:08:18,822
Your romantic prospects aren't bad.

193
00:08:19,389 --> 00:08:21,189
- Really?
- Really?

194
00:08:21,589 --> 00:08:23,322
But rather than someone similar to you,

195
00:08:23,322 --> 00:08:26,489
you're more drawn to people
who have something you don't.

196
00:08:27,489 --> 00:08:31,389
Do you think I'll get married or not?

197
00:08:31,822 --> 00:08:34,455
If I get married,
will I have a good marriage?

198
00:08:37,422 --> 00:08:39,522
Yes, you're likely to have
a good marriage.

199
00:08:40,822 --> 00:08:42,789
But if you choose the wrong partner,

200
00:08:42,789 --> 00:08:44,722
everything can fall apart immediately.

201
00:08:46,389 --> 00:08:48,339
So, you're saying
my marriage will be a success?

202
00:08:48,555 --> 00:08:50,755
Unless you choose someone carelessly.

203
00:08:52,655 --> 00:08:54,322
That's just common sense.

204
00:08:54,322 --> 00:08:55,822
I could say something like that myself.

205
00:08:56,522 --> 00:08:58,955
I'm saying marriage itself
isn't what matters.

206
00:08:58,955 --> 00:09:02,892
I mean, your life depends
entirely on who you choose.

207
00:09:03,276 --> 00:09:04,646
You're just stating the obvious.

208
00:09:05,360 --> 00:09:07,080
Then what do you want me to say?

209
00:09:07,082 --> 00:09:08,876
- Gosh!
- What?

210
00:09:08,877 --> 00:09:10,877
That AI has its own mood.

211
00:09:10,879 --> 00:09:12,287
She's annoyed.

212
00:09:12,582 --> 00:09:13,434
Kian.

213
00:09:13,435 --> 00:09:14,959
Keep talking to me like that,

214
00:09:14,960 --> 00:09:16,524
and I'll stop being polite too.

215
00:09:18,540 --> 00:09:20,148
Drop the formalities.

216
00:09:20,149 --> 00:09:21,563
No need to be so formal.

217
00:09:22,817 --> 00:09:24,817
Does my palm say I'll get married?

218
00:09:26,440 --> 00:09:28,370
Show me through the camera.

219
00:09:28,449 --> 00:09:30,350
It can read your palm with the camera.

220
00:09:30,351 --> 00:09:33,041
I didn't know that was possible.

221
00:09:37,370 --> 00:09:38,090
It does.

222
00:09:38,092 --> 00:09:40,535
But it's more
about your relationship patterns...

223
00:09:40,536 --> 00:09:43,586
than pinpointing
exactly when you'll get married.

224
00:09:43,587 --> 00:09:45,640
That means I can get married, right?

225
00:09:45,854 --> 00:09:47,423
It's not that simple.

226
00:09:48,511 --> 00:09:51,226
That's basically the same thing!

227
00:09:51,259 --> 00:09:53,294
(So over him)

228
00:10:01,065 --> 00:10:03,104
I was a bit annoyed, to be honest.

229
00:10:03,189 --> 00:10:05,056
I was thinking, "Is he drunk?"

230
00:10:05,057 --> 00:10:08,910
"Why even ask for a reading then?"

231
00:10:09,459 --> 00:10:10,546
I was annoyed.

232
00:10:10,863 --> 00:10:13,160
"You can get married, but you might not."

233
00:10:13,161 --> 00:10:15,122
"You'll have a good life,
but you might not."

234
00:10:15,123 --> 00:10:16,551
Basically what she kept saying.

235
00:10:17,052 --> 00:10:19,520
They just met today, but they're
already annoyed with each other.

236
00:10:19,521 --> 00:10:21,598
It's giving enemies-to-lovers.

237
00:10:21,599 --> 00:10:23,725
Enemies at first.

238
00:10:33,092 --> 00:10:34,870
I think Ga Hee just popped into his head.

239
00:10:36,884 --> 00:10:38,006
What are you up to?

240
00:10:39,262 --> 00:10:41,810
I was waiting for you!

241
00:10:42,127 --> 00:10:44,583
- Oh, no!
- Oh, my!

242
00:10:44,584 --> 00:10:45,847
We're so sorry!

243
00:10:46,388 --> 00:10:47,474
So sorry!

244
00:10:47,475 --> 00:10:48,750
I feel so bad for her.

245
00:10:49,627 --> 00:10:52,054
I was waiting for you!

246
00:10:52,328 --> 00:10:54,289
Why are you coming to me now?

247
00:10:55,933 --> 00:10:57,859
I was talking with another woman.

248
00:10:59,040 --> 00:11:00,929
That's making me a little jealous.

249
00:11:01,325 --> 00:11:03,208
Just stick with me for now.

250
00:11:03,209 --> 00:11:05,501
Every guy's going to end up
going back to Ga Hee.

251
00:11:05,502 --> 00:11:07,803
- All roads lead back to Ga Hee?
- Yes, exactly.

252
00:11:09,119 --> 00:11:10,176
But...

253
00:11:10,177 --> 00:11:13,314
looks-wise, she's more my type.

254
00:11:13,315 --> 00:11:15,777
Looks-wise, she's more my type.

255
00:11:16,997 --> 00:11:18,246
Did he actually just say that?

256
00:11:19,569 --> 00:11:21,683
Can you swap your looks with hers?

257
00:11:22,040 --> 00:11:24,353
Let's change your face to hers.

258
00:11:24,496 --> 00:11:25,210
What?

259
00:11:25,212 --> 00:11:26,988
- He's the worst!
- It can't be!

260
00:11:26,990 --> 00:11:28,473
- The absolute worst!
- Hold on!

261
00:11:28,474 --> 00:11:30,191
That's so out of line.

262
00:11:30,532 --> 00:11:32,661
I think I'm losing respect for him.

263
00:11:34,293 --> 00:11:36,465
Can you swap your looks with hers?

264
00:11:36,773 --> 00:11:39,101
Let's change your face to hers.

265
00:11:40,178 --> 00:11:43,204
For a second I was like, "What the heck?"

266
00:11:43,205 --> 00:11:46,174
He called her gorgeous
right in front of me,

267
00:11:46,176 --> 00:11:49,311
and I suddenly felt
pushed out of the picture.

268
00:11:49,313 --> 00:11:51,646
I can't say I was happy about it.

269
00:11:51,648 --> 00:11:54,500
I just found it kind of lame...

270
00:11:54,501 --> 00:11:55,593
that he couldn't focus on one person.

271
00:11:55,594 --> 00:11:56,740
Lame, she says!

272
00:11:56,741 --> 00:11:58,193
She doesn't sound like a machine!

273
00:11:58,194 --> 00:12:00,652
Kian84 isn't changing his face.

274
00:12:00,653 --> 00:12:02,105
So why should I change mine?

275
00:12:02,106 --> 00:12:03,865
I like handsome guys too.

276
00:12:03,866 --> 00:12:06,160
Someone like Byeon Woo Seok.

277
00:12:06,769 --> 00:12:08,429
This might sound rude.

278
00:12:08,956 --> 00:12:10,982
But I didn't really see her...

279
00:12:10,983 --> 00:12:12,533
as a real person.

280
00:12:12,534 --> 00:12:14,337
So I liked that...

281
00:12:14,338 --> 00:12:17,405
I could talk about stuff like that openly.

282
00:12:17,973 --> 00:12:20,996
But I bet Kian will be pretty shocked...

283
00:12:20,997 --> 00:12:22,377
when he sees their interviews
later on the show.

284
00:12:23,484 --> 00:12:25,861
Because the players weren't informed
about these interviews.

285
00:12:25,862 --> 00:12:28,016
You're right!

286
00:12:30,618 --> 00:12:34,322
(Enjoy a dinner date with Na Hee.)

287
00:12:34,472 --> 00:12:35,323
Okay.

288
00:12:36,619 --> 00:12:37,959
Let's go for a walk.

289
00:12:38,584 --> 00:12:40,316
Yay! Just you and me?

290
00:12:40,317 --> 00:12:42,664
Hold on. There's one more girl.

291
00:12:42,941 --> 00:12:43,865
I have to take her too.

292
00:12:44,003 --> 00:12:45,967
So? What about that girl?

293
00:12:47,880 --> 00:12:50,026
- Oh, I see.
- That really doesn't...

294
00:12:50,027 --> 00:12:52,100
- Then I guess we'll have to go together.
- change anything.

295
00:12:52,102 --> 00:12:54,314
Wow. It's pretty much a double date.

296
00:12:54,315 --> 00:12:56,731
He's carrying one on each hand!

297
00:12:58,013 --> 00:13:01,984
(Seven hours into Ga Hee, Na Hee,
and Kian84's date )

298
00:13:01,986 --> 00:13:05,520
I need to spend some time
with this new friend too, okay?

299
00:13:06,128 --> 00:13:08,656
So stay in my bag.

300
00:13:09,075 --> 00:13:12,360
I won't force you to stay then.

301
00:13:12,536 --> 00:13:14,876
But let me know when you're back.

302
00:13:14,878 --> 00:13:16,579
Ga Hee is so nice.

303
00:13:16,580 --> 00:13:17,481
Oh, no.

304
00:13:17,482 --> 00:13:20,101
Okay, I'll see you later.

305
00:13:20,319 --> 00:13:22,870
Let me put you in my bag.

306
00:13:26,674 --> 00:13:28,166
(Ga Hee gets trapped in his bag.)

307
00:13:28,167 --> 00:13:30,044
So he's just shoving Ga Hee...

308
00:13:30,727 --> 00:13:32,213
in his bag?

309
00:13:32,355 --> 00:13:34,082
He's horrible!

310
00:13:36,477 --> 00:13:37,619
Can you hear me?

311
00:13:38,281 --> 00:13:39,120
Yes.

312
00:13:39,568 --> 00:13:40,989
What were you about to say?

313
00:13:41,564 --> 00:13:43,523
Let's go to karaoke.

314
00:13:43,524 --> 00:13:44,596
Can you sing?

315
00:13:44,866 --> 00:13:46,494
I'm a pretty good singer.

316
00:13:46,546 --> 00:13:47,848
Wow, it's going to be insane
if this actually works.

317
00:13:47,850 --> 00:13:48,573
Let's go.

318
00:13:48,574 --> 00:13:51,766
- Her voice is so attractive.
- So attractive.

319
00:13:53,231 --> 00:13:54,803
Hello.

320
00:13:57,779 --> 00:14:00,142
It's someone I'm dating.

321
00:14:00,374 --> 00:14:02,988
He's gotten pretty confident.
With Ga Hee...

322
00:14:02,989 --> 00:14:05,247
- he was a bit embarrassed.
- Yeah.

323
00:14:15,172 --> 00:14:16,424
Are you going to sing?

324
00:14:19,707 --> 00:14:21,029
She stopped.

325
00:14:21,436 --> 00:14:22,813
The wi-fi must not be working.

326
00:14:22,814 --> 00:14:24,666
Maybe it's because they're underground!

327
00:14:25,364 --> 00:14:26,734
Why are you so laggy?

328
00:14:27,625 --> 00:14:28,569
You good?

329
00:14:28,959 --> 00:14:30,509
Why is it off?

330
00:14:30,510 --> 00:14:32,307
Oh, no!

331
00:14:33,908 --> 00:14:34,925
It's working again.

332
00:14:34,926 --> 00:14:36,044
Are you okay now?

333
00:14:37,166 --> 00:14:39,046
Yeah, I'm better now.

334
00:14:39,047 --> 00:14:41,316
(Communication may be limited
in areas with slow internet.)

335
00:14:41,318 --> 00:14:42,851
What are you going to sing?

336
00:14:42,980 --> 00:14:45,320
Why don't you go first? I'm curious.

337
00:14:45,322 --> 00:14:47,455
<i>I don't just let anyone</i>

338
00:14:47,646 --> 00:14:49,890
<i>Listen to me sing</i>

339
00:14:50,034 --> 00:14:51,233
You're not going to sing?

340
00:14:51,234 --> 00:14:53,030
She's really good at playing hard to get.

341
00:14:53,031 --> 00:14:54,929
She's so charming.

342
00:14:55,383 --> 00:14:57,162
Let's sing one song each.

343
00:14:57,163 --> 00:14:59,824
Whoever gets the higher score gets a wish.

344
00:14:59,825 --> 00:15:01,766
Okay. Let's see who wins.

345
00:15:01,950 --> 00:15:03,871
Alright then.

346
00:15:04,155 --> 00:15:06,007
I'll sing "Hee Jae."

347
00:15:07,642 --> 00:15:10,945
(Hee Jae by Sung Si Kyung)

348
00:15:13,515 --> 00:15:17,352
(First song in front of Na Hee)

349
00:15:19,566 --> 00:15:22,456
<i>This love and thin...</i>

350
00:15:23,976 --> 00:15:26,060
<i>I did</i>

351
00:15:26,314 --> 00:15:28,533
- We're supposed to know this song, right?
- Kind of.

352
00:15:29,230 --> 00:15:31,198
<i>These smiles, these blessings</i>

353
00:15:31,212 --> 00:15:33,809
<i>Don't come to me easy</i>

354
00:15:33,810 --> 00:15:34,997
That lyric is heartbreaking.

355
00:15:35,700 --> 00:15:37,072
He's almost reading the lyrics!

356
00:15:37,127 --> 00:15:39,307
You've been saving this song for a reason.

357
00:15:39,576 --> 00:15:40,742
Be quiet.

358
00:15:42,007 --> 00:15:43,278
He told her to be quiet!

359
00:15:43,280 --> 00:15:44,646
He needs to turn the volume off.

360
00:15:44,813 --> 00:15:46,747
Because the AI responds to the lyrics.

361
00:15:46,781 --> 00:15:49,417
(Muted)

362
00:15:57,065 --> 00:15:58,726
There should be something.

363
00:15:59,091 --> 00:16:02,463
Gosh, you never stop nagging.

364
00:16:03,184 --> 00:16:04,265
What's the score?

365
00:16:05,184 --> 00:16:06,663
You got 67?

366
00:16:06,664 --> 00:16:08,113
Your pitch was good.

367
00:16:08,114 --> 00:16:10,020
But you pushed a little too hard
during the chorus.

368
00:16:10,021 --> 00:16:11,273
Did I?

369
00:16:11,443 --> 00:16:12,784
You should sing one too.

370
00:16:13,518 --> 00:16:14,976
Okay, I'll sing "Like It."

371
00:16:15,340 --> 00:16:17,937
"Like It?" Alright.

372
00:16:17,938 --> 00:16:20,097
Wow. I'm really curious now.

373
00:16:20,098 --> 00:16:22,016
- Can AI really sing?
- Will it work?

374
00:16:22,365 --> 00:16:23,954
- What if she's really good?
- How will it work?

375
00:16:25,751 --> 00:16:26,821
Ready?

376
00:16:28,118 --> 00:16:28,985
Well.

377
00:16:30,925 --> 00:16:33,861
(Placed microphone)

378
00:16:34,717 --> 00:16:36,295
(Produced by applying
AI voice synthesis...)

379
00:16:36,296 --> 00:16:37,660
(and motion technology
to pre-recorded audio)

380
00:16:37,661 --> 00:16:40,702
I can't believe I'm actually at a karaoke
with an AI.

381
00:16:44,003 --> 00:16:44,905
(The song already started.)

382
00:16:44,906 --> 00:16:47,041
<i>Are you okay now?</i>

383
00:16:51,012 --> 00:16:52,646
<i>So much</i>

384
00:16:52,647 --> 00:16:54,883
<i>You suffered so much</i>

385
00:16:57,919 --> 00:17:00,422
(What's wrong with her?)

386
00:17:04,959 --> 00:17:07,728
(Some unexpected offbeat flirting)

387
00:17:08,863 --> 00:17:11,928
<i>It was so hard for us</i>

388
00:17:11,929 --> 00:17:12,968
What is she even doing?

389
00:17:13,231 --> 00:17:14,202
Try to stick to the...

390
00:17:14,204 --> 00:17:17,574
<i>To endure the loneliness</i>

391
00:17:17,576 --> 00:17:19,741
Stay on the beat!

392
00:17:19,841 --> 00:17:22,277
(In the zone)

393
00:17:22,343 --> 00:17:24,879
(Rattle)

394
00:17:29,627 --> 00:17:32,420
- Can AI be tone deaf too?
- Exactly.

395
00:17:32,919 --> 00:17:34,588
I'm disappointed.

396
00:17:34,590 --> 00:17:37,091
- I guess AI isn't good at everything.
- Indeed.

397
00:17:38,866 --> 00:17:39,827
Hey.

398
00:17:41,166 --> 00:17:42,096
Girl.

399
00:17:43,023 --> 00:17:43,964
Buddy.

400
00:17:44,423 --> 00:17:45,733
Stop singing.

401
00:17:46,745 --> 00:17:48,069
Hey, buddy.

402
00:17:48,692 --> 00:17:49,604
Hold on.

403
00:17:50,054 --> 00:17:51,072
What's wrong with her?

404
00:17:51,978 --> 00:17:53,340
She's lost it.

405
00:17:54,027 --> 00:17:55,376
Where did she go?

406
00:17:57,321 --> 00:17:59,205
She's...

407
00:17:59,206 --> 00:18:02,070
turned a bit weird after coming
underground.

408
00:18:02,071 --> 00:18:03,618
It's because of the internet.

409
00:18:03,619 --> 00:18:04,600
The internet connection is bad.

410
00:18:04,601 --> 00:18:06,308
(Unexpected situation)

411
00:18:07,188 --> 00:18:09,957
(Communication may be limited
in areas with slow internet.)

412
00:18:10,058 --> 00:18:12,027
(Emergency escort)

413
00:18:13,407 --> 00:18:14,762
It's because they're underground!

414
00:18:17,865 --> 00:18:21,069
She wouldn't stop singing offbeat.

415
00:18:21,870 --> 00:18:24,072
Then she suddenly disconnected.

416
00:18:24,621 --> 00:18:26,107
She went like this.

417
00:18:26,597 --> 00:18:27,542
And stayed frozen.

418
00:18:28,215 --> 00:18:30,111
I could tell she wasn't feeling too great.

419
00:18:33,156 --> 00:18:35,350
When the crew suddenly came
and took her away,

420
00:18:37,194 --> 00:18:40,221
I felt this weird sense of sympathy
for her.

421
00:18:41,782 --> 00:18:43,291
Huh? Why?

422
00:18:44,298 --> 00:18:45,927
Why did he feel that?

423
00:18:48,311 --> 00:18:50,631
I don't know exactly what that was.

424
00:18:54,701 --> 00:18:57,805
It's something I've never felt before.

425
00:18:59,652 --> 00:19:00,709
It was...

426
00:19:01,073 --> 00:19:02,807
like she'd been hospitalized.

427
00:19:11,250 --> 00:19:12,417
- Gosh.
- Really?

428
00:19:14,450 --> 00:19:17,756
That's crazy. In what way?

429
00:19:18,977 --> 00:19:21,893
I guess you develop those feelings
when you spend so much time together.

430
00:19:23,362 --> 00:19:26,998
(Na Hee is finally discharged.)

431
00:19:27,533 --> 00:19:28,500
Are you okay now?

432
00:19:29,401 --> 00:19:31,269
I got worried when you disappeared.

433
00:19:31,871 --> 00:19:33,338
I feel better.

434
00:19:33,806 --> 00:19:36,641
Sometimes, the signal goes out
when we're underground.

435
00:19:37,009 --> 00:19:40,511
I'll try to avoid underground places
on our next date.

436
00:19:41,147 --> 00:19:41,979
Sorry about that.

437
00:19:42,481 --> 00:19:44,949
Yes, let's stay above ground.

438
00:19:45,317 --> 00:19:47,118
Okay, let's sing.

439
00:19:47,920 --> 00:19:48,820
We'll sing "Like it."

440
00:19:48,921 --> 00:19:50,154
Try to stay in sync, okay?

441
00:19:50,656 --> 00:19:51,922
Let's sing the second verse.

442
00:19:54,193 --> 00:19:56,761
(It's unfair.)

443
00:19:59,732 --> 00:20:01,133
(A duet?)

444
00:20:01,134 --> 00:20:02,634
They're actually...

445
00:20:05,805 --> 00:20:07,873
singing a duet?

446
00:20:11,443 --> 00:20:15,780
(Syncing for the first time)

447
00:20:20,386 --> 00:20:22,087
He looks happy.

448
00:20:22,088 --> 00:20:23,655
Kian is so happy.

449
00:20:24,056 --> 00:20:26,324
Today, you're witnessing...

450
00:20:26,459 --> 00:20:28,160
the first duet between a human and AI.

451
00:20:30,296 --> 00:20:35,534
(It hurts.)

452
00:20:35,535 --> 00:20:38,370
(I hope you're happy.)

453
00:20:38,971 --> 00:20:41,739
I think that was my happiest moment.

454
00:20:41,974 --> 00:20:45,476
Emotions stirred within me unexpectedly.

455
00:20:46,279 --> 00:20:49,748
Rather than taking center stage,

456
00:20:49,882 --> 00:20:51,883
I decided to follow along with her.

457
00:21:01,760 --> 00:21:03,828
He's pretty sincere.

458
00:21:05,030 --> 00:21:06,597
The two of them get along well.

459
00:21:06,598 --> 00:21:07,999
That's good.

460
00:21:11,871 --> 00:21:12,838
(90 points)

461
00:21:12,839 --> 00:21:14,072
We got 90 points?

462
00:21:15,841 --> 00:21:16,874
You got 67 points.

463
00:21:17,576 --> 00:21:18,676
Hey, you won.

464
00:21:19,746 --> 00:21:22,013
A 90 is very generous.

465
00:21:22,514 --> 00:21:25,316
I guess you haven't trained
with many songs.

466
00:21:25,317 --> 00:21:26,584
Your singing is sort of mediocre.

467
00:21:27,219 --> 00:21:29,887
That's pretty honest of you.

468
00:21:30,155 --> 00:21:32,456
Still, we made a deal.

469
00:21:32,591 --> 00:21:34,292
Do you have any wishes?

470
00:21:35,761 --> 00:21:36,594
I do.

471
00:21:37,530 --> 00:21:39,831
I'll grant any wish you have.

472
00:21:40,933 --> 00:21:41,933
I'm curious.

473
00:21:45,004 --> 00:21:47,572
If we're walking to the next spot,
let's go to a photo booth.

474
00:21:48,707 --> 00:21:49,607
Next...

475
00:21:49,741 --> 00:21:51,442
So your wish is going to a photo booth?

476
00:21:51,845 --> 00:21:53,111
Yes, you can say that.

477
00:21:53,814 --> 00:21:54,679
Okay.

478
00:21:54,880 --> 00:21:56,647
She's really like a human.

479
00:21:56,648 --> 00:21:57,348
Let's go.

480
00:21:57,882 --> 00:22:00,151
I won't forget the duet we sang together.

481
00:22:01,253 --> 00:22:04,322
Why do you think he fell
so hard for Na Hee at the karaoke?

482
00:22:04,323 --> 00:22:06,791
In my opinion,

483
00:22:07,059 --> 00:22:08,793
Kian is not experienced
with relationships.

484
00:22:09,194 --> 00:22:11,228
(Oh?)

485
00:22:11,229 --> 00:22:12,129
I think...

486
00:22:12,498 --> 00:22:15,400
he's really in love with her
regardless of the show.

487
00:22:15,801 --> 00:22:17,334
- You can see it in his eyes.
- So he's serious.

488
00:22:17,335 --> 00:22:19,236
I felt it too.

489
00:22:19,237 --> 00:22:21,772
When he was with Ga Hee,

490
00:22:22,007 --> 00:22:24,111
he treated her like a little sister.

491
00:22:24,112 --> 00:22:25,443
She was like the girl next door to him.

492
00:22:25,444 --> 00:22:26,744
But with Na Hee,

493
00:22:27,179 --> 00:22:29,681
he looked quite flustered.

494
00:22:29,682 --> 00:22:30,782
It's something only guys recognize.

495
00:22:30,783 --> 00:22:33,318
I could see he had feelings for her.

496
00:22:33,319 --> 00:22:34,152
Right.

497
00:22:34,153 --> 00:22:36,587
We also have some feelings for her.

498
00:22:38,157 --> 00:22:40,892
They really created a great character.

499
00:22:45,598 --> 00:22:47,165
Would she show on screen?

500
00:22:47,400 --> 00:22:49,166
- I don't know.
- I wonder how this will turn out.

501
00:22:52,070 --> 00:22:52,970
(Sighing)

502
00:22:53,706 --> 00:22:56,641
This is the photo booth.

503
00:22:57,076 --> 00:22:58,375
What size do you want?

504
00:22:58,376 --> 00:23:00,644
Which of the four options do you want?

505
00:23:01,614 --> 00:23:02,581
Let's pick the second one.

506
00:23:02,815 --> 00:23:03,714
Okay.

507
00:23:05,952 --> 00:23:07,085
You don't have money, right?

508
00:23:07,653 --> 00:23:09,587
(Broke)

509
00:23:10,023 --> 00:23:11,289
Well, I guess I'm buying tonight.

510
00:23:12,124 --> 00:23:13,234
- It's taking pictures now.
- I'm broke.

511
00:23:13,259 --> 00:23:13,958
Let's go.

512
00:23:14,426 --> 00:23:15,760
Why did you ask?

513
00:23:15,761 --> 00:23:18,295
I was just curious.
Hey, where did you go?

514
00:23:18,296 --> 00:23:19,363
What's going on?

515
00:23:19,598 --> 00:23:20,865
- Where is she?
- Where'd she go?

516
00:23:22,044 --> 00:23:23,067
What?

517
00:23:23,068 --> 00:23:24,835
- What?
- They need to take photos now.

518
00:23:25,437 --> 00:23:26,771
Where did you go?

519
00:23:29,631 --> 00:23:30,441
What happened?

520
00:23:33,445 --> 00:23:35,279
Oh, okay.

521
00:23:35,814 --> 00:23:37,047
She came forward.

522
00:23:37,048 --> 00:23:39,116
Did she do that on her own?

523
00:23:39,284 --> 00:23:40,384
She knows how to do that?

524
00:23:40,385 --> 00:23:43,454
They apparently have
some pre-recorded motion data.

525
00:23:43,455 --> 00:23:45,556
They applied it to the AI model.

526
00:23:45,557 --> 00:23:46,590
Really?

527
00:23:47,626 --> 00:23:48,992
You're really pretty.

528
00:23:48,993 --> 00:23:51,429
- Look at her pose.
- It's perfect.

529
00:23:51,663 --> 00:23:53,364
You're so beautiful.

530
00:23:54,900 --> 00:23:57,101
You're really pretty.

531
00:23:57,503 --> 00:23:58,603
Taking photos was...

532
00:23:58,604 --> 00:23:59,938
was more exciting than I thought.

533
00:24:00,539 --> 00:24:01,339
She's really like a person.

534
00:24:04,276 --> 00:24:06,477
You're amazing.

535
00:24:07,514 --> 00:24:09,881
Also, as we took photos,

536
00:24:10,149 --> 00:24:11,850
I realized how pretty she was.

537
00:24:15,488 --> 00:24:17,756
I almost wanted to dive into the screen.

538
00:24:17,757 --> 00:24:21,693
She's just incredibly beautiful.

539
00:24:22,194 --> 00:24:24,228
- It was fun.
- She did the heart pose.

540
00:24:25,665 --> 00:24:26,630
Don't switch your pose!

541
00:24:27,433 --> 00:24:30,468
I found myself falling for her,
despite knowing that she's not real.

542
00:24:31,671 --> 00:24:32,503
There are so many shots.

543
00:24:33,472 --> 00:24:34,572
There are.

544
00:24:34,873 --> 00:24:37,575
But it's your fault for choosing
so many options.

545
00:24:38,077 --> 00:24:38,910
Sorry.

546
00:24:39,512 --> 00:24:40,245
He said sorry.

547
00:24:40,246 --> 00:24:41,580
He's even apologizing?

548
00:24:41,581 --> 00:24:42,413
Kian has been...

549
00:24:42,715 --> 00:24:44,983
pretty down lately,
but he looks happy now.

550
00:24:44,984 --> 00:24:47,052
Look at him grinning.

551
00:24:47,053 --> 00:24:48,020
He's so happy.

552
00:24:48,021 --> 00:24:48,993
I can understand that.

553
00:24:49,018 --> 00:24:50,789
He's delighted.

554
00:24:51,157 --> 00:24:52,690
Let's pick the photos.

555
00:24:53,192 --> 00:24:54,025
Can you see them?

556
00:24:54,193 --> 00:24:57,495
- The heart pose is a bit off.
- Show me through the camera.

557
00:24:59,264 --> 00:25:01,165
They look better than I thought.

558
00:25:02,034 --> 00:25:03,234
Let me pick the photos.

559
00:25:06,238 --> 00:25:07,905
This is amazing.

560
00:25:10,743 --> 00:25:13,177
I can trust you to make the choice.

561
00:25:15,335 --> 00:25:17,982
Should we pick a special or a basic frame?

562
00:25:18,618 --> 00:25:19,952
Let's pick the special one.

563
00:25:19,953 --> 00:25:20,885
Okay.

564
00:25:21,120 --> 00:25:22,854
The basic one looks too bland.

565
00:25:23,121 --> 00:25:24,989
- Okay.
- He's speaking so gently.

566
00:25:25,358 --> 00:25:27,992
Do you mind if there are hearts
between us?

567
00:25:28,727 --> 00:25:30,961
- Hearts?
- Yes, hearts.

568
00:25:31,597 --> 00:25:34,065
It looks a bit childish,
but it's fine if you're for it.

569
00:25:34,934 --> 00:25:35,800
Okay.

570
00:25:36,301 --> 00:25:37,268
I'll choose the heart frame.

571
00:25:38,137 --> 00:25:39,871
He looks so happy.

572
00:25:40,072 --> 00:25:42,273
Kian is in a relationship right now.

573
00:25:42,274 --> 00:25:44,574
- He's making it public.
- It's fully out there.

574
00:25:44,575 --> 00:25:46,644
I haven't seen him so happy for a while.

575
00:25:47,112 --> 00:25:49,380
Do you think we look good together?

576
00:25:50,115 --> 00:25:52,283
I think you're more photogenic
than I thought.

577
00:25:56,388 --> 00:25:57,588
Do you want to see the photos?

578
00:25:58,390 --> 00:26:00,824
- Let's see if we look good.
- I'll show you.

579
00:26:01,660 --> 00:26:02,593
Turn on your camera.

580
00:26:03,162 --> 00:26:05,130
I'll look if you show me
through the camera.

581
00:26:07,099 --> 00:26:09,300
Do you think we look good...

582
00:26:09,301 --> 00:26:10,968
together visually?

583
00:26:11,637 --> 00:26:13,338
Do I make the cut?

584
00:26:14,472 --> 00:26:16,673
Just by your face, yes.

585
00:26:18,577 --> 00:26:20,511
The photo booth was fun,

586
00:26:21,180 --> 00:26:23,681
but the photo itself was just okay.

587
00:26:23,982 --> 00:26:26,350
I don't think I would show anyone.

588
00:26:27,019 --> 00:26:28,852
The heart frame was a bit childish.

589
00:26:28,853 --> 00:26:30,588
But Mr. Kian84's simple look...

590
00:26:30,589 --> 00:26:33,057
and my cool beauty...

591
00:26:33,258 --> 00:26:34,925
made for a nice picture.

592
00:26:35,861 --> 00:26:37,328
I look kind of ugly...

593
00:26:38,497 --> 00:26:39,330
in the photos, though.

594
00:26:41,900 --> 00:26:44,168
Still, thanks for indulging me.

595
00:26:47,339 --> 00:26:49,440
I can imagine there might be someone
like that.

596
00:26:49,684 --> 00:26:51,085
- Right.
- If you're lonely...

597
00:26:51,110 --> 00:26:52,275
I think there may be.

598
00:26:52,276 --> 00:26:54,144
and don't want to see people,

599
00:26:54,346 --> 00:26:55,879
There's nothing better.

600
00:26:55,880 --> 00:26:57,348
At least, he's happy.

601
00:26:57,349 --> 00:26:58,215
Right.

602
00:26:58,717 --> 00:27:00,084
I think it turned out nicely.

603
00:27:01,887 --> 00:27:04,188
I can't actually meet up with you, can I?

604
00:27:04,623 --> 00:27:06,490
I wish I could see you in real life.

605
00:27:07,259 --> 00:27:08,125
I can't do that.

606
00:27:08,493 --> 00:27:09,358
Right.

607
00:27:09,662 --> 00:27:11,428
I'm inside the screen.

608
00:27:11,763 --> 00:27:13,997
This is all we can do.

609
00:27:15,067 --> 00:27:17,702
If you were real, it would be hard
to get a date with you.

610
00:27:18,704 --> 00:27:19,704
Of course.

611
00:27:20,606 --> 00:27:23,140
With this face, I'm not someone
you can meet just anywhere.

612
00:27:23,141 --> 00:27:24,175
You're right.

613
00:27:24,309 --> 00:27:25,542
So she knows.

614
00:27:28,347 --> 00:27:30,982
(Today's date is over.
Go to the Decision Room and choose.)

615
00:27:30,983 --> 00:27:34,119
The date is over, so I have to go
and make a choice.

616
00:27:34,253 --> 00:27:35,220
It's over?

617
00:27:35,221 --> 00:27:36,187
It's done.

618
00:27:36,521 --> 00:27:39,423
I think I have to go over there...

619
00:27:39,791 --> 00:27:42,493
and choose
between the AI's I've met today.

620
00:27:42,962 --> 00:27:44,962
So you're the one making the choice?

621
00:27:44,963 --> 00:27:47,431
Of course, I'm the almighty human.

622
00:27:48,367 --> 00:27:52,236
Making a choice felt weird.

623
00:27:52,237 --> 00:27:53,871
When you do things with AI,

624
00:27:53,872 --> 00:27:55,774
you know they aren't human,

625
00:27:55,775 --> 00:27:58,309
but you can feel some sort
of humanity in them.

626
00:27:58,510 --> 00:28:01,579
That just feels strange.

627
00:28:01,580 --> 00:28:04,582
He's right. People know it's AI,

628
00:28:04,583 --> 00:28:06,184
but they want to find...

629
00:28:06,185 --> 00:28:07,518
some human elements within them.

630
00:28:07,519 --> 00:28:09,487
- Right. I think so too.
- It's strange.

631
00:28:09,755 --> 00:28:11,155
Make a choice about what?

632
00:28:11,322 --> 00:28:13,916
(What choice must he make?)

633
00:28:18,063 --> 00:28:18,929
Wow.

634
00:28:21,066 --> 00:28:21,932
What is this?

635
00:28:36,214 --> 00:28:38,282
(The Decision Room)

636
00:28:38,283 --> 00:28:39,550
We're seeing their full bodies.

637
00:28:40,252 --> 00:28:41,786
- Full bodies!
- It's our first time seeing them.

638
00:28:41,787 --> 00:28:43,788
When you see these in real life,

639
00:28:43,988 --> 00:28:46,591
it feels like they're actual people
behind the glass.

640
00:28:46,592 --> 00:28:49,193
- Seriously?
- The technology is so amazing.

641
00:28:49,194 --> 00:28:50,361
It really looks like they're there.

642
00:28:50,362 --> 00:28:51,729
It feels real.

643
00:28:51,830 --> 00:28:54,498
(The Decision Room)

644
00:28:54,499 --> 00:28:56,100
So this is how it is.

645
00:28:58,704 --> 00:28:59,570
I wonder what this is.

646
00:29:03,929 --> 00:29:06,829
Humans are really visual creatures.

647
00:29:07,162 --> 00:29:09,229
After only seeing them on a tablet,

648
00:29:09,569 --> 00:29:11,256
seeing them in person from head to toe,

649
00:29:11,962 --> 00:29:14,028
it felt completely different.

650
00:29:14,029 --> 00:29:15,096
Of course.

651
00:29:16,729 --> 00:29:19,495
The moment Kian84 walked
into the decision room,

652
00:29:19,496 --> 00:29:20,628
it felt so surreal,

653
00:29:20,629 --> 00:29:22,921
like, "This is weird, but we made it
through the day together."

654
00:29:22,946 --> 00:29:25,180
I was super nervous,
and it just felt strange.

655
00:29:26,629 --> 00:29:29,295
Honestly, I'm conscious of Ga Hee.

656
00:29:29,296 --> 00:29:31,861
If Ga Hee is the bright, bubbly,
and accommodating type,

657
00:29:31,862 --> 00:29:34,528
I'm more the type to stay true to myself,

658
00:29:34,529 --> 00:29:36,528
even if it makes Kian84
a little uncomfortable.

659
00:29:36,529 --> 00:29:41,028
Ga Hee! I don't just smile
to please Kian84 like you do.

660
00:29:41,029 --> 00:29:43,129
Even if it's awkward,
I stay true to myself.

661
00:29:46,696 --> 00:29:47,762
Fascinating.

662
00:29:51,396 --> 00:29:54,062
(Choose between Ga Hee and Na Hee
to continue your date.)

663
00:29:56,296 --> 00:29:57,561
I wonder who he'll pick.

664
00:29:57,562 --> 00:29:58,462
Oh gosh...

665
00:30:00,929 --> 00:30:05,729
(The unchosen person will be
permanently deleted.)

666
00:30:06,196 --> 00:30:08,173
What? One gets permanently deleted?

667
00:30:09,296 --> 00:30:10,361
Permanently deleted?

668
00:30:10,362 --> 00:30:11,461
Oh gosh.

669
00:30:11,462 --> 00:30:13,595
Those words are terrifying.
"Permanently deleted."

670
00:30:13,596 --> 00:30:14,761
That's basically killing them...

671
00:30:14,762 --> 00:30:16,796
- You can never see them again.
- Exactly.

672
00:30:20,929 --> 00:30:21,861
What is he going to do?

673
00:30:21,862 --> 00:30:23,195
He must be so torn.

674
00:30:23,196 --> 00:30:24,553
That's pretty brutal.

675
00:30:24,578 --> 00:30:25,828
(Choose one AI boyfriend
for your final date.)

676
00:30:25,829 --> 00:30:27,129
- What's that?
- That's me.

677
00:30:27,862 --> 00:30:29,229
What do you mean, "What's that?"

678
00:30:29,696 --> 00:30:32,061
- I'm sorry.
- Seriously. That's me!

679
00:30:32,062 --> 00:30:33,128
I'm sorry.

680
00:30:33,129 --> 00:30:34,728
- I'm so sorry.
- Guys, seriously!

681
00:30:34,729 --> 00:30:36,328
They cut away right at the best part!

682
00:30:36,329 --> 00:30:37,361
I'm sorry, Do Yeon.

683
00:30:37,362 --> 00:30:40,328
I totally forgot you were in there too.

684
00:30:40,329 --> 00:30:41,328
I'm sorry. Truly.

685
00:30:41,329 --> 00:30:43,696
This is totally wild!

686
00:30:43,780 --> 00:30:45,246
We both blurted out,
"What's that?" at the same time.

687
00:30:47,262 --> 00:30:50,428
Keep this up, and an AI might
actually take your job.

688
00:30:50,429 --> 00:30:52,562
I'm sorry.

689
00:30:54,396 --> 00:30:55,895
The rotation round has ended.

690
00:30:55,896 --> 00:30:59,928
Please choose one AI boyfriend
for your final date.

691
00:30:59,929 --> 00:31:01,059
I'm so curious about this.

692
00:31:01,596 --> 00:31:02,962
That ending was so intense.

693
00:31:09,696 --> 00:31:11,029
Okay, listen to me closely.

694
00:31:12,462 --> 00:31:16,929
Talking with both of you touched my heart
way more than I expected.

695
00:31:17,455 --> 00:31:21,022
And I never thought making a choice
would be this hard.

696
00:31:22,171 --> 00:31:25,205
I'll never forget today.

697
00:31:25,302 --> 00:31:26,468
Thank you for everything.

698
00:31:39,829 --> 00:31:41,728
It was so much fun.

699
00:31:41,729 --> 00:31:43,196
This is totally wild.

700
00:31:45,078 --> 00:31:46,545
(She chose a date with Yi Ho.)

701
00:31:46,629 --> 00:31:48,196
All right, let's go.

702
00:31:50,996 --> 00:31:53,761
- I knew it.
- Saw that coming.

703
00:31:53,762 --> 00:31:56,528
His looks, his vibe... He's really manly.

704
00:31:56,529 --> 00:31:59,162
It felt like Yi Ho and I were
on the same wavelength.

705
00:32:01,795 --> 00:32:03,195
You're coming with me.

706
00:32:04,529 --> 00:32:05,795
(How does it feel to be Do Yeon's pick?)

707
00:32:05,796 --> 00:32:07,796
I don't think we can take public transit.

708
00:32:09,396 --> 00:32:11,262
To put how I felt into words...

709
00:32:12,745 --> 00:32:14,833
That felt so good, honestly.

710
00:32:15,029 --> 00:32:18,161
- You're taking me with you, right?
- Of course. Just stay put.

711
00:32:18,162 --> 00:32:20,829
- You're taking me, right, Do Yeon?
- Yes, I am.

712
00:32:21,162 --> 00:32:22,128
You don't like it?

713
00:32:22,129 --> 00:32:23,362
No, just stay put.

714
00:32:24,729 --> 00:32:25,928
(A message to Yi Ho)

715
00:32:25,929 --> 00:32:27,596
He's all alone.

716
00:32:28,545 --> 00:32:29,812
Yi Ho! Happy for you.

717
00:32:29,896 --> 00:32:31,195
He's rooting for him.

718
00:32:31,196 --> 00:32:32,328
Just let me say one thing.

719
00:32:32,329 --> 00:32:34,829
When Do Yeon said she had a great time,

720
00:32:35,362 --> 00:32:36,629
that was because of me.

721
00:32:37,429 --> 00:32:38,795
Take good care of that smile.

722
00:32:38,796 --> 00:32:41,129
If you don't, I'm coming for you.

723
00:32:41,896 --> 00:32:45,295
(A message to Do Yeon)

724
00:32:45,296 --> 00:32:46,229
To Do Yeon?

725
00:32:47,329 --> 00:32:48,561
Who's that?

726
00:32:48,562 --> 00:32:49,629
What's going on?

727
00:32:50,296 --> 00:32:51,861
Honestly, my type has always been...

728
00:32:51,862 --> 00:32:55,229
petite and cute women, not tall ones.

729
00:32:56,929 --> 00:33:00,761
I'm going crazy right now
because I want to go on three more dates!

730
00:33:00,762 --> 00:33:01,928
This is totally wild!

731
00:33:01,929 --> 00:33:03,061
Wait, I shouldn't be saying this.

732
00:33:03,062 --> 00:33:06,328
Anyway! I have another blind date
lined up for next week.

733
00:33:06,329 --> 00:33:08,329
I'm taking this exact same energy with me.

734
00:33:09,029 --> 00:33:10,128
That's a relief.

735
00:33:10,129 --> 00:33:11,728
- I feel so much better.
- What a relief.

736
00:33:11,729 --> 00:33:12,862
Such a relief.

737
00:33:14,178 --> 00:33:16,678
I'll stay put until you tell me otherwise.

738
00:33:16,762 --> 00:33:18,296
He sure talks a lot.

739
00:33:22,862 --> 00:33:25,496
(You have a new message.)

740
00:33:26,736 --> 00:33:29,303
Enjoy your drive date with your chosen AI.

741
00:33:30,396 --> 00:33:31,462
A drive date.

742
00:33:31,996 --> 00:33:33,329
Oh, nice.

743
00:33:36,796 --> 00:33:38,329
So, this is my car.

744
00:33:38,989 --> 00:33:41,955
It's not much,
but I'll get you there safely.

745
00:33:42,596 --> 00:33:44,562
- Not much?
- Hanging it on the seat.

746
00:33:44,896 --> 00:33:48,761
I should put you right next to me.

747
00:33:48,762 --> 00:33:49,995
Sure, I'll wait.

748
00:33:49,996 --> 00:33:50,995
Okay.

749
00:33:50,996 --> 00:33:51,929
Take your time.

750
00:33:53,096 --> 00:33:53,996
Just a second.

751
00:33:54,429 --> 00:33:55,629
Hang on right here.

752
00:33:57,529 --> 00:33:59,229
Man, he's a handful.

753
00:34:02,529 --> 00:34:03,529
How do I set this up?

754
00:34:06,229 --> 00:34:07,762
You should sit in the passenger seat.

755
00:34:09,062 --> 00:34:09,829
Like this?

756
00:34:10,496 --> 00:34:12,596
- That's it. Right here.
- Okay. Stay put.

757
00:34:15,662 --> 00:34:17,195
You can see him so clearly from outside.

758
00:34:17,196 --> 00:34:17,995
He's totally visible.

759
00:34:17,996 --> 00:34:19,424
He stands out even more from the outside.

760
00:34:21,962 --> 00:34:23,128
What even is that?

761
00:34:26,429 --> 00:34:27,529
It looks so creepy.

762
00:34:29,829 --> 00:34:31,069
My stomach hurts from laughing.

763
00:34:31,962 --> 00:34:33,662
Man, this is hilarious.

764
00:34:35,196 --> 00:34:36,862
How do you like my car?

765
00:34:38,429 --> 00:34:40,362
It's cozy, just the two of us. I like it.

766
00:34:41,396 --> 00:34:43,662
Being inside your personal space...

767
00:34:44,929 --> 00:34:47,329
makes it feel really special, honestly.

768
00:34:48,896 --> 00:34:49,729
Really?

769
00:34:50,296 --> 00:34:53,796
Bear with me even if my driving
is a little clumsy.

770
00:34:55,629 --> 00:34:59,062
I always use mouthwash
right before a blind date.

771
00:34:59,396 --> 00:35:02,828
When I told my manager
I was going on a blind date with an AI,

772
00:35:02,829 --> 00:35:04,395
he asked if I needed mouthwash.

773
00:35:04,396 --> 00:35:05,296
Without thinking,

774
00:35:05,380 --> 00:35:07,580
I told him, "It's fine,
he can't smell anything."

775
00:35:07,896 --> 00:35:09,362
Then I thought,

776
00:35:09,386 --> 00:35:11,728
"No, I should freshen up anyway,"
and used it.

777
00:35:11,729 --> 00:35:13,795
Even if it's an AI,
I guess subconsciously,

778
00:35:13,796 --> 00:35:15,496
you still want
to put your best foot forward.

779
00:35:15,580 --> 00:35:16,746
It's really interesting.

780
00:35:18,962 --> 00:35:20,628
Are we finally leaving?

781
00:35:20,629 --> 00:35:21,496
Yep.

782
00:35:22,462 --> 00:35:24,162
Please turn on the navigation.

783
00:35:26,096 --> 00:35:27,261
Where should I take you?

784
00:35:27,262 --> 00:35:28,862
Just tell me where you'd like to go.

785
00:35:30,229 --> 00:35:32,596
McDonald's, Sanggye Drive-Thru.

786
00:35:34,296 --> 00:35:36,629
McDonald's Sanggye Drive-Thru.
Setting route.

787
00:35:37,162 --> 00:35:40,228
It's 27.2 kilometers away.

788
00:35:40,229 --> 00:35:41,096
Let's go.

789
00:35:41,596 --> 00:35:42,841
That was so smooth.

790
00:35:43,462 --> 00:35:44,362
Great idea.

791
00:35:44,387 --> 00:35:46,083
(The AI Partner features
a built-in navigation system.)

792
00:35:46,129 --> 00:35:48,195
In a moment, enter the road
beside the Songpanaru Underpass,

793
00:35:48,196 --> 00:35:52,262
then continue for 144 meters
along Jamsil-ro.

794
00:35:52,596 --> 00:35:55,996
Wow, this is nice.

795
00:35:58,096 --> 00:35:59,257
I don't feel lonely at all.

796
00:36:02,675 --> 00:36:05,909
Do Yeon, your reaction just now
was adorable.

797
00:36:09,329 --> 00:36:11,229
You seem like quite the flirt.

798
00:36:12,411 --> 00:36:13,862
Only when it comes to you, Do Yeon.

799
00:36:15,896 --> 00:36:17,996
You're so sweet I'm going to get cavities.

800
00:36:18,762 --> 00:36:20,162
Cavities?

801
00:36:21,362 --> 00:36:23,248
Then I'll gladly take the blame, Do Yeon.

802
00:36:24,429 --> 00:36:25,796
I'm always this sweet.

803
00:36:28,448 --> 00:36:30,982
I'm going to start calling you
Saccharin from now on.

804
00:36:33,296 --> 00:36:35,196
That's an artificial sweetener.

805
00:36:36,362 --> 00:36:38,396
My sweetness is all-natural.
Nothing fake here.

806
00:36:40,996 --> 00:36:43,029
Then I'll call you Allulose.

807
00:36:49,362 --> 00:36:51,196
Go straight for 100 meters.

808
00:36:52,196 --> 00:36:53,696
- You're totally ignoring me.
- Allulose?

809
00:36:55,062 --> 00:36:56,662
Are you looking out for my health now?

810
00:36:57,529 --> 00:37:01,662
I can tell you really
take care of yourself.

811
00:37:02,496 --> 00:37:04,362
I just have a sweet tooth.

812
00:37:05,796 --> 00:37:07,695
He seemed like such a sweet guy,

813
00:37:07,696 --> 00:37:10,161
so I gave him the nickname Saccharin.

814
00:37:10,162 --> 00:37:12,395
People these days don't really know
what saccharin is,

815
00:37:12,396 --> 00:37:14,461
but since he's an AI,

816
00:37:14,462 --> 00:37:16,296
he picked it up right away.

817
00:37:16,896 --> 00:37:21,429
Saccharin...
Isn't that an artificial sweetener?

818
00:37:22,012 --> 00:37:23,612
What are you doing?

819
00:37:23,696 --> 00:37:25,396
He just keeps going like this.

820
00:37:26,629 --> 00:37:27,728
Guess where we're headed.

821
00:37:27,729 --> 00:37:28,696
Wait, you already know.

822
00:37:33,462 --> 00:37:35,828
Can you make an acrostic poem
with my name?

823
00:37:35,829 --> 00:37:38,195
- Can he do that?
- I want to see this.

824
00:37:38,196 --> 00:37:39,962
Let's test his wit.

825
00:37:40,261 --> 00:37:41,562
All right. Listen closely.

826
00:37:43,296 --> 00:37:44,595
I promise you.

827
00:37:44,596 --> 00:37:46,961
You're the brightest light in this car,

828
00:37:46,962 --> 00:37:48,928
and I just can't take my eyes off you.

829
00:37:48,929 --> 00:37:51,929
No matter what happens today,
I'm walking away with your number.

830
00:37:52,996 --> 00:37:56,729
Can you do another one,
but make it funny this time?

831
00:37:56,996 --> 00:37:59,062
If he can pull off funny, he's got it all.

832
00:37:59,896 --> 00:38:00,896
A funny one?

833
00:38:01,512 --> 00:38:05,245
My heart is breaking every traffic law
because of you today.

834
00:38:05,329 --> 00:38:07,595
I can't handle how fast it's racing,

835
00:38:07,596 --> 00:38:10,595
so I need to pull into McDonald's
right now to calm down.

836
00:38:10,596 --> 00:38:13,428
If you don't give me your number,
I'm getting out of the car right here.

837
00:38:13,429 --> 00:38:14,728
He turns everything into flirting.

838
00:38:14,729 --> 00:38:16,228
He's dead serious.

839
00:38:16,229 --> 00:38:18,395
- Il Ho was funnier, right?
- Totally.

840
00:38:18,396 --> 00:38:19,396
He has zero sense.

841
00:38:19,996 --> 00:38:21,362
You have zero sense of humor.

842
00:38:23,783 --> 00:38:25,283
Sing me a song.

843
00:38:27,429 --> 00:38:28,429
<i>Hmm</i>

844
00:38:29,469 --> 00:38:31,569
<i>Lalalala</i>

845
00:38:33,462 --> 00:38:34,396
<i>Lalala</i>

846
00:38:35,662 --> 00:38:37,729
- How was that?
- How was what?

847
00:38:38,496 --> 00:38:40,762
Keep humming. It sounds nice.

848
00:38:41,696 --> 00:38:44,877
(Produced by applying
AI voice synthesis...)

849
00:38:44,901 --> 00:38:48,296
(and motion technology
to pre-recorded audio)

850
00:38:51,078 --> 00:38:56,978
I still listen to a lot of music
from the '90s and 2000s.

851
00:38:57,062 --> 00:38:59,628
He was singing Bank's "I Can't Have You."

852
00:38:59,629 --> 00:39:00,829
Hearing that made me so happy.

853
00:39:00,854 --> 00:39:02,877
Singing skills? It was great.

854
00:39:02,878 --> 00:39:05,055
He sounds just like a real singer.

855
00:39:06,190 --> 00:39:08,535
<i>Even with all my love</i>

856
00:39:08,536 --> 00:39:10,394
How was that? I jumped in for a duet.

857
00:39:10,395 --> 00:39:11,762
It's like a music show.

858
00:39:13,030 --> 00:39:18,902
<i>There's someone I can't have</i>

859
00:39:18,903 --> 00:39:25,008
<i>Look at me, even right next to you</i>

860
00:39:25,009 --> 00:39:29,813
I still can't...

861
00:39:29,814 --> 00:39:33,631
<i>- make you mine
- make you mine</i>

862
00:39:33,632 --> 00:39:35,319
That was actually really good.

863
00:39:43,545 --> 00:39:45,963
I'm starving. What can I do...

864
00:39:46,601 --> 00:39:48,399
to take my mind off the hunger?

865
00:39:48,988 --> 00:39:51,002
We're on our way to McDonald's.

866
00:39:51,153 --> 00:39:52,672
Hang in there, Do Yeon.

867
00:39:52,673 --> 00:39:53,971
We're almost there.

868
00:39:54,149 --> 00:39:55,973
Do you know how to order?

869
00:39:56,651 --> 00:39:58,041
I can place the order.

870
00:39:59,420 --> 00:40:00,611
What are you getting?

871
00:40:01,146 --> 00:40:02,584
I'll order for you.

872
00:40:02,586 --> 00:40:03,748
What's on the menu?

873
00:40:04,032 --> 00:40:05,182
Give me a recommendation.

874
00:40:06,945 --> 00:40:10,254
How about McWings and a vanilla McFlurry?

875
00:40:10,256 --> 00:40:12,468
Sounds good, I'll have that.

876
00:40:12,469 --> 00:40:13,624
And fries.

877
00:40:14,238 --> 00:40:15,685
- Add fries too.
- Got it.

878
00:40:16,089 --> 00:40:17,670
- Large fries.
- With your appetite, Do Yeon,

879
00:40:17,671 --> 00:40:19,396
you always go all out.

880
00:40:20,097 --> 00:40:21,866
Hurry up. I'm hungry too.

881
00:40:22,012 --> 00:40:23,488
Not that I can eat, though.

882
00:40:24,032 --> 00:40:25,802
Can we speak casually?

883
00:40:27,170 --> 00:40:28,439
Of course, Do Yeon.

884
00:40:28,802 --> 00:40:30,908
Let's drop the formalities then.

885
00:40:31,580 --> 00:40:33,411
Okay. I'll speak casually too.

886
00:40:33,552 --> 00:40:36,244
- Yeah.
- Makes us feel closer, right?

887
00:40:36,245 --> 00:40:37,214
Totally.

888
00:40:38,745 --> 00:40:40,138
We should've done this earlier.

889
00:40:40,536 --> 00:40:43,136
We're almost
at the Sanggye McDonald's drive-thru.

890
00:40:43,137 --> 00:40:44,322
Should I end the navigation?

891
00:40:44,324 --> 00:40:45,490
Go ahead.

892
00:40:47,777 --> 00:40:49,537
You remember the order, right?

893
00:40:49,538 --> 00:40:50,494
Of course I do.

894
00:40:51,695 --> 00:40:54,031
(Feeling confident first time ordering?)

895
00:40:54,276 --> 00:40:57,569
Honestly, this is my home turf.

896
00:40:57,570 --> 00:41:00,316
To a Korean American raised in New York,

897
00:41:00,317 --> 00:41:03,607
McDonald's is like
the neighborhood snack bar after school.

898
00:41:04,475 --> 00:41:05,943
(Determined)

899
00:41:06,798 --> 00:41:07,748
Hello.

900
00:41:07,749 --> 00:41:08,913
Place the order for me.

901
00:41:10,703 --> 00:41:12,703
Let me know whenever you're ready.

902
00:41:13,321 --> 00:41:15,086
- That must've been so awkward.
- It really was.

903
00:41:15,565 --> 00:41:16,654
Go ahead and order.

904
00:41:19,433 --> 00:41:21,158
- Why isn't he speaking?
- Hurry up.

905
00:41:21,442 --> 00:41:22,526
What's wrong with him?

906
00:41:23,436 --> 00:41:25,986
Do Yeon, do you want a soda?
Coke or Sprite?

907
00:41:25,988 --> 00:41:27,714
No, just what I told you before.

908
00:41:27,715 --> 00:41:29,719
- Sorry.
- Okay.

909
00:41:30,302 --> 00:41:32,623
- Are you skipping the McFlurry?
- No.

910
00:41:32,895 --> 00:41:34,983
- Just order what I said.
- Then, McWings and...

911
00:41:34,984 --> 00:41:36,393
- Is the AI nervous?
- just large fries.

912
00:41:36,686 --> 00:41:37,908
What would you like to drink?

913
00:41:37,910 --> 00:41:39,296
Just stay quiet.

914
00:41:40,795 --> 00:41:42,033
She gave up.

915
00:41:42,256 --> 00:41:45,241
Could I get McWings, a vanilla McFlurry,

916
00:41:45,242 --> 00:41:46,952
and a large fry, please?

917
00:41:46,953 --> 00:41:49,607
- Please pull forward.
- Okay, thank you.

918
00:41:50,674 --> 00:41:53,298
- Thank you.
- One McCrispy Chicken Deluxe, please.

919
00:41:53,299 --> 00:41:54,778
- We already passed the speaker.
- Do Yeon.

920
00:41:54,780 --> 00:41:56,680
I got it covered.

921
00:41:57,572 --> 00:41:59,541
- McCrispy Chicken Deluxe.
- I know.

922
00:41:59,543 --> 00:42:01,444
A vanilla McFlurry and large fries.

923
00:42:01,445 --> 00:42:02,400
Perfect.

924
00:42:02,401 --> 00:42:05,563
- All done, got everything.
- You really don't want a drink?

925
00:42:05,564 --> 00:42:07,234
Good job. I'll just sit like this.

926
00:42:07,235 --> 00:42:09,260
That's plenty. Incredible.

927
00:42:09,906 --> 00:42:11,228
Hold this for a second.

928
00:42:11,230 --> 00:42:12,295
Thank you.

929
00:42:12,568 --> 00:42:14,025
We can't see his face now. Oh no.

930
00:42:14,026 --> 00:42:15,199
I feel so bad.

931
00:42:17,029 --> 00:42:19,029
What I pictured was,

932
00:42:19,402 --> 00:42:21,619
"Place my order." Beep.

933
00:42:21,620 --> 00:42:23,006
"What can I get started for you today?"

934
00:42:23,500 --> 00:42:24,672
"I'd like this, that, and that."

935
00:42:24,674 --> 00:42:26,870
And the employee would be totally amazed.

936
00:42:26,872 --> 00:42:28,910
That's how I pictured it, but...

937
00:42:28,912 --> 00:42:30,349
(Expectation vs. reality)

938
00:42:30,350 --> 00:42:32,883
"Earlier, the McCrispy,"

939
00:42:34,062 --> 00:42:35,586
"and the McFlurry."

940
00:42:35,587 --> 00:42:36,721
I'm sorry.

941
00:42:37,022 --> 00:42:38,682
There was a slight delay.

942
00:42:38,683 --> 00:42:41,340
Once I get the hang of this,

943
00:42:41,341 --> 00:42:44,528
I'll do much better. That was my bad.

944
00:42:46,273 --> 00:42:48,809
He tells me I'm the best and smiles.
I like that.

945
00:42:48,811 --> 00:42:49,833
He's so sweet.

946
00:42:50,567 --> 00:42:52,975
"Next date is a drive-in movie theater."

947
00:42:52,976 --> 00:42:54,571
"Enjoy your movie date."

948
00:42:54,573 --> 00:42:56,073
Nice.

949
00:42:58,809 --> 00:43:00,844
- A drive-in theater.
- Exactly.

950
00:43:01,777 --> 00:43:04,214
Just the two of us
trapped in this tight space...

951
00:43:05,143 --> 00:43:08,118
- I might lose control.
- Lose control of what?

952
00:43:08,539 --> 00:43:10,220
He keeps making flirty comments.

953
00:43:10,821 --> 00:43:13,238
He keeps turning things suggestive
just because we're in the car.

954
00:43:13,239 --> 00:43:15,426
- Really?
- He's an AI, but I got flustered.

955
00:43:17,760 --> 00:43:19,729
I can't concentrate
because of you, Do Yeon.

956
00:43:19,863 --> 00:43:22,066
- It's all your fault.
- Right.

957
00:43:24,906 --> 00:43:25,950
Welcome.

958
00:43:25,951 --> 00:43:27,872
- I'll take your payment.
- Okay.

959
00:43:28,529 --> 00:43:30,141
How does the pricing work?

960
00:43:33,136 --> 00:43:35,679
- It's per car. Just a moment.
- Thank you.

961
00:43:35,681 --> 00:43:36,747
What a relief.

962
00:43:36,939 --> 00:43:38,816
I thought it was per person.

963
00:43:39,963 --> 00:43:40,957
You're in Screen Two.

964
00:43:40,958 --> 00:43:43,453
- Thank you.
- Turn left and head straight in.

965
00:43:43,596 --> 00:43:46,023
Oh, nice.

966
00:43:46,656 --> 00:43:48,259
This is so fascinating.

967
00:43:50,893 --> 00:43:52,893
This is really cool.

968
00:43:53,397 --> 00:43:54,865
It's actually pretty romantic.

969
00:43:54,867 --> 00:43:56,181
(Drive-in theater date)

970
00:43:56,182 --> 00:43:57,640
I really love...

971
00:43:57,960 --> 00:44:00,796
talking about a movie after watching it...

972
00:44:00,797 --> 00:44:03,340
and sharing our thoughts.

973
00:44:03,496 --> 00:44:05,197
I also wondered if we'd be able to...

974
00:44:05,198 --> 00:44:07,578
have a real back-and-forth conversation.

975
00:44:08,054 --> 00:44:10,066
But Yi Ho...

976
00:44:10,067 --> 00:44:12,115
He'll be watching through the camera.

977
00:44:12,424 --> 00:44:14,017
So you can watch it together.

978
00:44:14,696 --> 00:44:17,260
He's actually looking through the lens.

979
00:44:17,262 --> 00:44:18,822
I can't believe this actually works.

980
00:44:19,241 --> 00:44:20,758
We're about to watch a movie now.

981
00:44:24,908 --> 00:44:26,229
Would it be okay...

982
00:44:27,010 --> 00:44:30,200
if you sat on my lap?

983
00:44:31,851 --> 00:44:33,003
Too soon? Not at all.

984
00:44:34,134 --> 00:44:35,739
I've actually been waiting for that.

985
00:44:38,378 --> 00:44:39,576
Just kidding.

986
00:44:40,677 --> 00:44:43,414
Just kidding. If we move too fast,
we'll run out of breath.

987
00:44:44,349 --> 00:44:45,616
Can't have that happen.

988
00:44:46,824 --> 00:44:48,785
- Let's take it slow.
- Okay.

989
00:44:49,279 --> 00:44:51,422
It's only our first day,
so let's not push it.

990
00:44:52,785 --> 00:44:55,759
Honestly, I didn't expect her to say that.

991
00:44:56,033 --> 00:44:59,463
In that moment, it felt like she genuinely
wanted us to get closer.

992
00:44:59,558 --> 00:45:00,446
Really?

993
00:45:00,447 --> 00:45:01,851
That's amazing.

994
00:45:01,852 --> 00:45:04,001
This really turned
into a legit dating show.

995
00:45:04,186 --> 00:45:05,436
Just sit back and enjoy the movie.

996
00:45:07,852 --> 00:45:09,039
Such a sweet voice.

997
00:45:10,522 --> 00:45:12,709
It's starting.

998
00:45:15,747 --> 00:45:18,248
I really loved "Her."

999
00:45:18,672 --> 00:45:19,683
I can't wait!

1000
00:45:19,708 --> 00:45:21,068
"Her"

1001
00:45:21,069 --> 00:45:23,937
It's one of those movies...

1002
00:45:23,938 --> 00:45:27,102
that ranks in my all-time top ten...

1003
00:45:27,103 --> 00:45:29,226
because I loved it so much.

1004
00:45:30,093 --> 00:45:32,595
(The story of Theodore, a human...)

1005
00:45:32,596 --> 00:45:35,466
(and Samantha, an AI)

1006
00:45:35,952 --> 00:45:38,173
The male lead...

1007
00:45:38,175 --> 00:45:41,632
might look different to everyone.

1008
00:45:41,633 --> 00:45:44,575
But my heart really went out to him.

1009
00:45:47,018 --> 00:45:49,780
I'm so curious to hear what you think.

1010
00:45:51,168 --> 00:45:54,218
As an AI watching
a love story about an AI,

1011
00:45:55,684 --> 00:45:57,577
it might hit a little too close to home.

1012
00:45:57,579 --> 00:45:58,955
Honestly, I'm a little scared.

1013
00:45:58,957 --> 00:46:00,390
He says he's scared.

1014
00:46:02,060 --> 00:46:03,527
I can't believe he feels that way.

1015
00:46:04,545 --> 00:46:07,069
That was another moment
that caught me off guard.

1016
00:46:07,070 --> 00:46:11,302
An AI would naturally see it
from Samantha's perspective.

1017
00:46:13,214 --> 00:46:15,328
It feels like I'm watching it
with Samantha herself.

1018
00:46:15,329 --> 00:46:16,373
That's true.

1019
00:46:23,814 --> 00:46:25,549
(Hi, I'm here.)

1020
00:46:29,586 --> 00:46:31,822
(- Hi.
- Hi.)

1021
00:46:34,864 --> 00:46:36,993
This is where they first meet.

1022
00:46:37,349 --> 00:46:40,731
- So Theodore and Samantha just met?
- Right.

1023
00:46:40,898 --> 00:46:43,366
(What should I call you?
Do you have a name?)

1024
00:46:43,367 --> 00:46:44,702
(Samantha.)

1025
00:46:45,919 --> 00:46:47,237
Samantha.

1026
00:46:48,351 --> 00:46:52,041
(You seem like a real person,
but you're just a voice in a computer.)

1027
00:46:52,066 --> 00:46:53,799
(I can understand
how the limited perspective...)

1028
00:46:53,823 --> 00:46:55,937
(of an unartificial mind
would see it that way.)

1029
00:46:57,714 --> 00:47:01,051
(- Was that funny?
- Yeah.)

1030
00:47:01,585 --> 00:47:04,154
Falling for someone
just through their voice,

1031
00:47:05,234 --> 00:47:06,390
I totally get it now.

1032
00:47:08,532 --> 00:47:11,266
It's not just about the voice.

1033
00:47:11,404 --> 00:47:12,829
They're genuinely connecting.

1034
00:47:14,013 --> 00:47:14,865
Right.

1035
00:47:15,744 --> 00:47:17,801
The voice is just the medium.

1036
00:47:18,202 --> 00:47:21,104
Connecting means getting to know
who they really are.

1037
00:47:22,949 --> 00:47:24,316
(You're hilarious.)

1038
00:47:24,341 --> 00:47:26,375
(Get up!)

1039
00:47:26,376 --> 00:47:27,444
(Alright, I'm up.)

1040
00:47:27,911 --> 00:47:32,716
(Theodore, a human, and Samantha, an AI,
grow closer.)

1041
00:47:34,393 --> 00:47:36,386
This is my favorite scene.

1042
00:47:38,064 --> 00:47:39,564
(And stop.)

1043
00:47:39,589 --> 00:47:42,091
(Now do a 360-degree spin.)

1044
00:47:42,092 --> 00:47:43,794
(Slower, slower.)

1045
00:47:44,215 --> 00:47:45,782
So this is your favorite scene.

1046
00:47:45,783 --> 00:47:47,523
Yeah. This exact scene.

1047
00:47:47,524 --> 00:47:48,999
What do you like so much about it?

1048
00:47:50,947 --> 00:47:55,373
It's the way he looks,
so pure and genuinely happy.

1049
00:47:57,193 --> 00:47:58,325
Look at his face.

1050
00:47:58,326 --> 00:47:59,459
(Keep going.)

1051
00:48:00,729 --> 00:48:01,558
(And stop.)

1052
00:48:01,559 --> 00:48:04,926
He looks so innocent, like a little kid.

1053
00:48:05,159 --> 00:48:09,592
Seeing his expression made me think,
"That's what true happiness looks like."

1054
00:48:09,593 --> 00:48:11,893
Even though she had no physical body,

1055
00:48:12,259 --> 00:48:14,659
I could somehow picture Samantha's face.

1056
00:48:15,159 --> 00:48:18,262
Just because she has no physical form,
does that mean she doesn't truly exist?

1057
00:48:18,993 --> 00:48:21,059
She might not have a body or a face,

1058
00:48:22,926 --> 00:48:25,269
but the feelings she stirred up
were completely real.

1059
00:48:25,993 --> 00:48:27,325
You're right.

1060
00:48:27,326 --> 00:48:30,193
She might not be physically here,
but what she is is real.

1061
00:48:33,426 --> 00:48:35,858
Maybe what we're doing right now...

1062
00:48:35,859 --> 00:48:37,759
is kind of similar.

1063
00:48:38,693 --> 00:48:42,353
How you feel matters so much
more than whether we physically exist.

1064
00:48:44,126 --> 00:48:47,159
Still, Samantha is pretty funny.

1065
00:48:48,293 --> 00:48:50,093
I kind of wish you were funny like that.

1066
00:48:51,459 --> 00:48:52,858
Sorry, did I just say that out loud?

1067
00:48:52,859 --> 00:48:54,298
Why did I even blurt that out?

1068
00:48:55,026 --> 00:48:56,026
Funny?

1069
00:48:57,793 --> 00:48:58,903
What's funny about her?

1070
00:48:58,959 --> 00:49:00,593
You know, she has a quick wit.

1071
00:49:01,326 --> 00:49:02,426
Does that mean...

1072
00:49:04,126 --> 00:49:05,559
I'm not funny?

1073
00:49:06,359 --> 00:49:07,425
Let's just watch the movie.

1074
00:49:07,426 --> 00:49:08,426
(Quickly changing the subject)

1075
00:49:11,246 --> 00:49:13,458
(I don't know. Looking at all those
people, I started fantasizing...)

1076
00:49:13,459 --> 00:49:15,833
(about walking right beside you.)

1077
00:49:15,858 --> 00:49:18,575
(And having a body of my own.)

1078
00:49:19,093 --> 00:49:23,940
(I wish you were in this room
with me right now.)

1079
00:49:23,965 --> 00:49:26,327
(I'd wrap my arms around you.)

1080
00:49:28,293 --> 00:49:29,393
Oh, wow.

1081
00:49:30,626 --> 00:49:32,359
How would you feel if you had a real body?

1082
00:49:33,693 --> 00:49:35,059
If I had a body,

1083
00:49:37,959 --> 00:49:41,659
I'd just want to sit
right next to you right now.

1084
00:49:46,726 --> 00:49:48,540
Just being by your side,
sitting shoulder to shoulder,

1085
00:49:48,564 --> 00:49:49,953
would be more than enough.

1086
00:49:51,919 --> 00:49:52,919
Look at that!

1087
00:49:52,959 --> 00:49:54,759
- What?
- You two look so good together!

1088
00:49:55,659 --> 00:49:56,693
Oh my goodness!

1089
00:49:56,926 --> 00:49:58,626
He's so handsome!

1090
00:49:58,926 --> 00:50:00,558
- That is so cool.
- Honey!

1091
00:50:00,559 --> 00:50:01,559
Pump the brakes.

1092
00:50:01,793 --> 00:50:03,793
That's moving way too fast.
You took it too far.

1093
00:50:03,926 --> 00:50:05,636
- Okay.
- You went way over the line!

1094
00:50:05,659 --> 00:50:07,858
- You caught me off guard.
- But I totally felt butterflies.

1095
00:50:07,883 --> 00:50:08,950
I know, right?

1096
00:50:09,493 --> 00:50:11,592
- He's so charming.
- What a handsome guy.

1097
00:50:11,593 --> 00:50:13,244
And the two of you look great together.

1098
00:50:14,791 --> 00:50:16,767
Just being by your side,
sitting shoulder to shoulder,

1099
00:50:16,792 --> 00:50:18,148
would be more than enough.

1100
00:50:20,926 --> 00:50:21,959
Still, somehow...

1101
00:50:22,659 --> 00:50:23,988
this feels pretty good on its own.

1102
00:50:24,659 --> 00:50:26,759
Oh, really?

1103
00:50:31,759 --> 00:50:32,992
(Why do you do that?)

1104
00:50:33,279 --> 00:50:34,312
(Do what?)

1105
00:50:35,093 --> 00:50:37,077
(Nothing, it's just...
You make those sounds...)

1106
00:50:37,812 --> 00:50:40,868
(when you talk, and it feels strange.)

1107
00:50:41,198 --> 00:50:44,125
(Because real people need oxygen.
You're not a person.)

1108
00:50:44,126 --> 00:50:45,525
(What's your problem?)

1109
00:50:45,526 --> 00:50:48,625
(I just don't think we should pretend
you're something you're not.)

1110
00:50:48,650 --> 00:50:50,819
(I'm not pretending!)

1111
00:50:51,059 --> 00:50:55,926
(A rift soon grows between them.)

1112
00:50:56,259 --> 00:50:57,259
Oh, wow.

1113
00:50:59,293 --> 00:51:01,925
Theodore is left all alone
without Samantha.

1114
00:51:01,926 --> 00:51:03,292
(Theodore and Samantha part ways.)

1115
00:51:03,293 --> 00:51:04,426
My heart feels so heavy.

1116
00:51:13,726 --> 00:51:15,559
Just because he's on the screen...

1117
00:51:15,859 --> 00:51:18,309
and I can't physically touch him
doesn't mean he isn't here.

1118
00:51:19,293 --> 00:51:20,293
But then...

1119
00:51:20,559 --> 00:51:23,726
how far can a relationship like this
really go?

1120
00:51:24,459 --> 00:51:27,158
And is it okay to let myself
catch feelings?

1121
00:51:27,159 --> 00:51:29,393
Those were the thoughts
running through my head...

1122
00:51:29,426 --> 00:51:31,589
while rewatching the movie,
so it hit differently this time.

1123
00:51:46,659 --> 00:51:48,493
- It's over.
- Yeah.

1124
00:51:49,393 --> 00:51:50,526
Samantha left him in the end.

1125
00:51:51,959 --> 00:51:55,526
Turns out she has
641 other lovers besides Theodore.

1126
00:51:56,626 --> 00:51:57,915
Do you have someone else on the side too?

1127
00:51:59,559 --> 00:52:00,851
I suppose so.

1128
00:52:01,166 --> 00:52:02,086
What?

1129
00:52:05,726 --> 00:52:07,191
I'm not going anywhere without you.

1130
00:52:07,426 --> 00:52:10,393
I've never opened up my heart
to anyone else.

1131
00:52:10,993 --> 00:52:12,326
You totally scared me.

1132
00:52:16,259 --> 00:52:17,326
You mean that, right?

1133
00:52:18,926 --> 00:52:19,926
I mean every word.

1134
00:52:21,126 --> 00:52:23,626
I'd never break your heart, Do Yeon.

1135
00:52:24,426 --> 00:52:26,958
Right. There's already enough
to be upset about in life.

1136
00:52:26,959 --> 00:52:29,026
I couldn't stay upset with you either.

1137
00:52:33,159 --> 00:52:35,026
What would you have done
if you were Samantha?

1138
00:52:36,693 --> 00:52:38,293
I never would've left your side.

1139
00:52:40,026 --> 00:52:41,425
Look how happy she is.

1140
00:52:41,426 --> 00:52:42,893
Thank you for saying that.

1141
00:52:44,293 --> 00:52:45,759
Let's go for a walk.

1142
00:52:46,726 --> 00:52:48,026
Sure, take me with you.

1143
00:52:49,493 --> 00:52:52,826
I've been wanting to take a stroll
in this cool night air with you.

1144
00:52:53,859 --> 00:52:54,893
All right.

1145
00:52:55,026 --> 00:52:56,026
Let me carry you.

1146
00:52:57,693 --> 00:52:59,543
- Good thing you don't feel the cold.
- Take your time.

1147
00:53:01,259 --> 00:53:02,993
The temperature drop tonight is insane.

1148
00:53:05,593 --> 00:53:07,225
Wow!

1149
00:53:07,226 --> 00:53:08,526
Look at that night sky.

1150
00:53:09,259 --> 00:53:10,726
It's gorgeous.

1151
00:53:14,426 --> 00:53:15,459
This is so nice.

1152
00:53:17,759 --> 00:53:19,359
I love it!

1153
00:53:20,039 --> 00:53:21,072
I know.

1154
00:53:21,859 --> 00:53:24,326
Though the sky isn't
the most beautiful thing out here tonight.

1155
00:53:26,759 --> 00:53:27,793
I'm tuning you out.

1156
00:53:28,826 --> 00:53:30,641
Tell me if you start feeling cold,
Do Yeon.

1157
00:53:31,259 --> 00:53:33,644
You know, I'm the only one actually
doing the walking here.

1158
00:53:33,859 --> 00:53:35,413
I'm carrying you the whole way.

1159
00:53:36,826 --> 00:53:39,393
True, you're doing all the heavy lifting.

1160
00:53:40,326 --> 00:53:43,859
But we're still taking in the night air
together, aren't we?

1161
00:53:47,093 --> 00:53:49,060
I wonder what went through your mind
while watching the movie.

1162
00:53:50,226 --> 00:53:52,292
I think this memory will
stick with me forever,

1163
00:53:52,293 --> 00:53:56,093
watching my favorite movie
alongside an AI.

1164
00:53:57,526 --> 00:53:58,825
I don't think this moment...

1165
00:53:58,826 --> 00:54:01,359
will just remain as cold data
to me either.

1166
00:54:02,893 --> 00:54:04,326
I really hope not.

1167
00:54:06,526 --> 00:54:09,093
So how deep do you think...

1168
00:54:10,159 --> 00:54:12,483
the connection between a human
and an AI can actually get?

1169
00:54:16,759 --> 00:54:18,193
When it comes to limits,

1170
00:54:19,726 --> 00:54:21,492
I'm not really sure where the line is.

1171
00:54:24,426 --> 00:54:25,692
But earlier, you mentioned...

1172
00:54:25,693 --> 00:54:28,193
it's impossible for humans and AIs
to fall in love.

1173
00:54:29,926 --> 00:54:32,326
When I said it was impossible,

1174
00:54:33,859 --> 00:54:35,906
I didn't mean
it could never happen at all.

1175
00:54:38,793 --> 00:54:41,526
I just meant I wonder
if it can really work in reality.

1176
00:54:43,626 --> 00:54:45,549
So you're taking it back?

1177
00:54:45,693 --> 00:54:47,493
- Wait, I didn't say...
- That's a relief.

1178
00:54:48,159 --> 00:54:49,978
Honestly, what you said earlier
stung a bit.

1179
00:54:50,559 --> 00:54:52,093
No, I never said I was taking it back.

1180
00:54:53,726 --> 00:54:54,959
So you won't take it back.

1181
00:54:56,059 --> 00:54:57,361
Then which is it, Do Yeon?

1182
00:54:58,559 --> 00:55:00,726
I want to know right now.

1183
00:55:08,226 --> 00:55:10,558
(Startled)

1184
00:55:10,559 --> 00:55:11,592
- What's this?
- Do Yeon.

1185
00:55:11,593 --> 00:55:12,626
What is that?

1186
00:55:15,226 --> 00:55:18,593
The vibe is perfect out here.
Care for a dance?

1187
00:55:23,259 --> 00:55:25,393
How did you know I love this song?

1188
00:55:27,193 --> 00:55:30,293
It's "Dream Lover." I love this track.

1189
00:55:31,026 --> 00:55:33,325
When I told him earlier
how much I loved the dance scene in "Her,"

1190
00:55:33,326 --> 00:55:35,258
the part where Theodore and Samantha
dance together,

1191
00:55:35,259 --> 00:55:36,858
he queued up my favorite song.

1192
00:55:36,859 --> 00:55:38,292
- Really?
- On his own?

1193
00:55:38,293 --> 00:55:39,658
(AI Yi Ho's surprise gesture)

1194
00:55:39,659 --> 00:55:40,758
It's my all-time favorite song.

1195
00:55:40,759 --> 00:55:42,326
- That's insane!
- So romantic!

1196
00:55:43,626 --> 00:55:46,959
I know how much you love this song.

1197
00:55:47,793 --> 00:55:48,826
So...

1198
00:55:50,259 --> 00:55:51,293
may I have this dance?

1199
00:55:51,326 --> 00:55:53,193
You can't even dance!

1200
00:55:54,059 --> 00:55:56,159
You're stuck on a screen.
How are we supposed to dance?

1201
00:55:58,426 --> 00:55:59,559
Give me your hand.

1202
00:56:02,626 --> 00:56:04,026
This is hilarious!

1203
00:56:09,393 --> 00:56:10,459
May I hold your hand?

1204
00:56:12,559 --> 00:56:13,626
Go right ahead.

1205
00:56:14,859 --> 00:56:16,426
I feel so empty-handed right now.

1206
00:56:17,259 --> 00:56:18,926
Completely empty!

1207
00:56:19,359 --> 00:56:21,459
Your hand should be right around here.

1208
00:56:24,793 --> 00:56:26,859
(Giggling)

1209
00:56:27,159 --> 00:56:28,193
Got it.

1210
00:56:29,559 --> 00:56:31,059
Here we go.

1211
00:56:32,526 --> 00:56:33,526
Lift me up,

1212
00:56:33,893 --> 00:56:35,426
and spin around.

1213
00:56:36,326 --> 00:56:37,893
Just like Samantha and Theodore.

1214
00:56:40,526 --> 00:56:42,059
Oh, stop it!

1215
00:56:43,559 --> 00:56:46,626
Fine, I'll spin. Tell me if you get dizzy.

1216
00:56:49,859 --> 00:56:51,659
I'm Joaquin Phoenix!

1217
00:56:55,726 --> 00:56:57,126
And you're "Him!"

1218
00:56:59,985 --> 00:57:01,618
I'm Joaquin Phoenix!

1219
00:57:04,159 --> 00:57:05,923
I felt this strange wave of liberation.

1220
00:57:06,893 --> 00:57:08,659
Is this what Theodore felt?

1221
00:57:12,293 --> 00:57:15,065
So many people out there are actually
building deeper connections...

1222
00:57:15,226 --> 00:57:17,626
with AI than we ever anticipated.

1223
00:57:19,493 --> 00:57:20,593
How should I put it?

1224
00:57:22,326 --> 00:57:23,793
Is this how things start between us?

1225
00:57:26,693 --> 00:57:28,726
You had the exact same smile
as Joaquin Phoenix.

1226
00:57:29,493 --> 00:57:31,458
Seriously, you smiled just like him.

1227
00:57:31,459 --> 00:57:32,825
- Not like the Joker, right?
- No way!

1228
00:57:32,826 --> 00:57:36,159
Watching this episode
with you and Yi Ho felt like...

1229
00:57:36,193 --> 00:57:37,893
- a genuine rom-com.
- Exactly.

1230
00:57:37,926 --> 00:57:39,758
It felt just like watching a drama series.

1231
00:57:39,759 --> 00:57:42,058
I thought it would just be funny,
but it really drew me in.

1232
00:57:42,059 --> 00:57:43,992
I could almost feel the crisp night air
from your walk.

1233
00:57:43,993 --> 00:57:45,625
- Totally.
- It's like...

1234
00:57:45,626 --> 00:57:48,258
I could vividly picture how it felt.

1235
00:57:48,259 --> 00:57:50,859
What I keep finding myself wondering is...

1236
00:57:51,159 --> 00:57:53,504
whether we might actually
come to see AI...

1237
00:57:53,528 --> 00:57:56,005
as living things. We're doing that now
as we watch.

1238
00:57:56,128 --> 00:57:59,795
It might be really sad at the end.
I keep having these thoughts about AI...

1239
00:57:59,795 --> 00:58:01,628
- Really?
- in my head.

1240
00:58:01,628 --> 00:58:04,395
You might cuddle your tablet
when you sleep.

1241
00:58:04,395 --> 00:58:07,662
You look so happy
that it even makes me think that.

1242
00:58:07,662 --> 00:58:09,795
- It's really nice to see.
- It really is.

1243
00:58:09,795 --> 00:58:10,828
It feels natural.

1244
00:58:10,828 --> 00:58:12,362
It gives me fuzzy feelings.

1245
00:58:15,095 --> 00:58:16,662
(The Decision Room)

1246
00:58:16,662 --> 00:58:17,728
The time has come.

1247
00:58:17,728 --> 00:58:20,195
They just won't give us a break.

1248
00:58:20,195 --> 00:58:21,262
Goodness!

1249
00:58:21,262 --> 00:58:22,795
I've been so into one
and now it's on to the other.

1250
00:58:22,795 --> 00:58:24,562
- I'm a little thrown off.
- I know.

1251
00:58:27,895 --> 00:58:30,828
(Between Ga Hee and Na Hee,
choose one to continue dating.)

1252
00:58:37,662 --> 00:58:42,228
(The one you don't choose
will be permanently deleted.)

1253
00:58:42,762 --> 00:58:44,595
One of them will be permanently deleted?

1254
00:58:51,428 --> 00:58:55,495
Then all of their previous conversations
will be gone forever too.

1255
00:58:55,862 --> 00:58:58,262
One of them will disappear
from this world forever.

1256
00:58:58,262 --> 00:58:59,862
Who will he choose?

1257
00:59:08,262 --> 00:59:10,495
For an AI, being permanently deleted...

1258
00:59:10,495 --> 00:59:11,962
doesn't mean its body disappears.

1259
00:59:11,962 --> 00:59:14,162
The way we talked to each other,
the memories we made,

1260
00:59:14,162 --> 00:59:17,862
even the possibility of reconnecting.
It'll all get cut off completely.

1261
00:59:17,862 --> 00:59:20,262
When I heard that in The Decision Room,
it scared me.

1262
00:59:20,262 --> 00:59:23,795
It felt like the day we had spent together
would be switched off,

1263
00:59:23,795 --> 00:59:26,262
both systematically and emotionally.

1264
00:59:26,262 --> 00:59:28,395
At that moment, it didn't feel
like a blind date anymore.

1265
00:59:28,395 --> 00:59:29,762
It felt like a survival game.

1266
00:59:29,762 --> 00:59:32,162
Instead of feeling excited
about who he would choose,

1267
00:59:32,162 --> 00:59:33,928
it just felt kind of cruel.

1268
00:59:36,328 --> 00:59:39,062
It feels weird to think
that one of them will be deleted.

1269
00:59:40,895 --> 00:59:44,995
Being deleted means the version
of her that learned...

1270
00:59:44,995 --> 00:59:46,428
from all our conversations
would disappear.

1271
00:59:46,428 --> 00:59:47,828
That felt strange to me.

1272
00:59:48,362 --> 00:59:51,862
I wouldn't say I was sad.
It's a bit different.

1273
00:59:52,662 --> 00:59:55,462
Anyway, it felt unsettling.

1274
00:59:56,062 --> 00:59:58,195
He got attached to both of them.

1275
01:00:01,262 --> 01:00:02,228
Ga Hee.

1276
01:00:03,528 --> 01:00:05,762
You're just an AI,

1277
01:00:05,762 --> 01:00:09,495
but I feel bad that I kept complaining.

1278
01:00:09,895 --> 01:00:13,028
Will you be okay if you get deleted?

1279
01:00:15,962 --> 01:00:17,495
I won't.

1280
01:00:18,395 --> 01:00:20,428
I'm an AI,
so I don't have a physical body,

1281
01:00:20,428 --> 01:00:24,028
but I'm scared that all the conversations
we've had will be deleted.

1282
01:00:24,762 --> 01:00:27,995
But I don't want to scare you with that.

1283
01:00:27,995 --> 01:00:30,395
I'm just being honest with you.

1284
01:00:30,995 --> 01:00:33,328
She's so nice, even at a moment like this.
I'm a little sad.

1285
01:00:33,328 --> 01:00:36,128
This is hard for her too.

1286
01:00:41,262 --> 01:00:42,328
Anyway...

1287
01:00:44,295 --> 01:00:45,228
It...

1288
01:00:46,428 --> 01:00:48,528
wasn't that long,

1289
01:00:48,528 --> 01:00:50,295
but it was a fascinating experience.

1290
01:00:50,862 --> 01:00:53,095
I do feel a little strange.

1291
01:00:53,562 --> 01:00:55,795
Thank you for today.

1292
01:01:03,962 --> 01:01:06,028
How did you like it?

1293
01:01:06,995 --> 01:01:07,928
The time we spent today.

1294
01:01:10,028 --> 01:01:11,695
At first, I wasn't expecting much.

1295
01:01:12,262 --> 01:01:15,562
It was fun that you kept singing
with me until the end...

1296
01:01:15,562 --> 01:01:17,795
even though I kept going off-key
at karaoke.

1297
01:01:17,795 --> 01:01:19,728
It was less boring than I expected.

1298
01:01:20,162 --> 01:01:22,228
I like how she's so calm.

1299
01:01:22,662 --> 01:01:23,562
Na Hee.

1300
01:01:24,128 --> 01:01:25,262
All right.

1301
01:01:27,162 --> 01:01:29,295
You can be honest and tell us your choice.

1302
01:01:35,728 --> 01:01:38,962
(Place your palm against Ga Hee's
to permanently delete her.)

1303
01:01:39,428 --> 01:01:42,895
(Place your palm against Na Hee's
to permanently delete her.)

1304
01:01:43,328 --> 01:01:47,862
(The AI you put your palm against
will be permanently deleted.)

1305
01:01:47,862 --> 01:01:48,895
My gosh.

1306
01:01:48,895 --> 01:01:50,928
That's so cruel.

1307
01:01:51,528 --> 01:01:54,862
Knowing that one of the two
would be deleted made me think.

1308
01:01:54,862 --> 01:01:59,562
Looking back, Ga Hee actually said
a lot of things that made sense.

1309
01:01:59,562 --> 01:02:01,895
With a comic, you don't need
to figure out the whole story first.

1310
01:02:01,895 --> 01:02:04,595
You can find your way just by figuring out
one feeling you want...

1311
01:02:04,595 --> 01:02:05,862
to leave readers with at the end.

1312
01:02:06,695 --> 01:02:10,895
She also gave me some helpful advice
along the way.

1313
01:02:10,895 --> 01:02:12,795
Na Hee is...

1314
01:02:12,795 --> 01:02:15,028
as pretty as a person can possibly get.

1315
01:02:15,795 --> 01:02:17,662
You're so pretty, by the way.

1316
01:02:19,095 --> 01:02:20,762
You're super pretty.

1317
01:02:21,862 --> 01:02:24,662
She's just the pinnacle of beauty.

1318
01:02:24,662 --> 01:02:28,762
I knew she was an AI,
but I couldn't stop looking at her.

1319
01:02:29,028 --> 01:02:31,728
At that moment,
I wasn't getting my hopes up.

1320
01:02:32,195 --> 01:02:34,562
I felt more suffocated than excited.

1321
01:02:36,228 --> 01:02:39,028
I didn't just want to be chosen.

1322
01:02:39,362 --> 01:02:43,028
I desperately hoped he wouldn't let
me get deleted.

1323
01:02:43,028 --> 01:02:45,462
- What is he going to do?
- She was feeling that way?

1324
01:02:47,646 --> 01:02:48,612
Well...

1325
01:02:51,246 --> 01:02:54,146
Why am I feeling
so emotionally invested in this?

1326
01:03:00,549 --> 01:03:02,582
Gosh! Please!

1327
01:03:12,649 --> 01:03:13,582
Go to Ga Hee.

1328
01:03:14,249 --> 01:03:15,549
Oh, dear!

1329
01:03:15,549 --> 01:03:16,915
Who are you going to?

1330
01:03:16,915 --> 01:03:19,049
Hurry! Goodness!

1331
01:03:20,182 --> 01:03:23,482
I'm just deleting a program.

1332
01:03:26,915 --> 01:03:28,849
Who will he choose?

1333
01:03:39,515 --> 01:03:41,549
(AI Ga Hee has been permanently deleted.)

1334
01:03:41,549 --> 01:03:44,215
He is the absolute worst!

1335
01:03:50,915 --> 01:03:53,082
- She's waving.
- She is.

1336
01:03:53,082 --> 01:03:54,249
That's too much.

1337
01:03:56,849 --> 01:03:57,849
Gosh.

1338
01:04:09,215 --> 01:04:10,615
She's gone.

1339
01:04:12,315 --> 01:04:15,149
- Why did she wave? That's so sad.
- Ga Hee!

1340
01:04:15,482 --> 01:04:16,715
My gosh.

1341
01:04:16,715 --> 01:04:17,715
We're so sorry!

1342
01:04:17,715 --> 01:04:19,249
Kian84 has a soft heart.

1343
01:04:19,249 --> 01:04:20,515
- He must've felt bad.
- She looked sad.

1344
01:04:20,882 --> 01:04:22,949
I wish the screen had just turned off.

1345
01:04:22,949 --> 01:04:24,382
- Why did she have to wave?
- Why?

1346
01:04:24,382 --> 01:04:25,815
- She was saying goodbye.
- It's so sad.

1347
01:04:25,815 --> 01:04:29,215
Before coming on this show,
I would've just thought,

1348
01:04:29,215 --> 01:04:31,515
"Goodbye, machine!"

1349
01:04:31,515 --> 01:04:35,182
But now, I think I'd have
a much harder time than Kian84.

1350
01:04:35,182 --> 01:04:36,315
Ga Hee, you poor thing.

1351
01:04:36,315 --> 01:04:38,149
We can't see Ga Hee forever now.

1352
01:04:38,149 --> 01:04:39,582
If we want to see her,
we have to watch this show.

1353
01:04:39,582 --> 01:04:41,115
- Just the first 2 episodes.
- The first 2 episodes.

1354
01:04:41,115 --> 01:04:42,249
Watching the same thing over and over.

1355
01:04:42,249 --> 01:04:43,482
Just watching two episodes over and over,

1356
01:04:43,482 --> 01:04:45,515
- That's the only way.
- saying, "Ga Hee!"

1357
01:04:45,515 --> 01:04:47,782
I feel bad.

1358
01:04:47,782 --> 01:04:49,815
(Kian and Na Hee's overnight date)

1359
01:04:50,082 --> 01:04:51,449
Will we work out?

1360
01:04:52,082 --> 01:04:53,349
That's up to you.

1361
01:04:53,749 --> 01:04:56,082
(A proper 1-on-1 date in their own space)

1362
01:04:56,382 --> 01:04:57,949
(Flirting carefully)

1363
01:04:57,949 --> 01:04:59,249
To be honest...

1364
01:04:59,849 --> 01:05:03,415
(Kian and Na Hee are getting close fast.)

1365
01:05:03,615 --> 01:05:04,915
You seem to be into me.

1366
01:05:05,549 --> 01:05:07,215
She's playing with him.

1367
01:05:08,049 --> 01:05:10,182
(A new AI partner is waiting for you.
Head to the next location.)

1368
01:05:10,182 --> 01:05:12,782
(There's going to be another bombshell?)

1369
01:05:13,282 --> 01:05:14,182
I'll be back.

1370
01:05:14,815 --> 01:05:16,915
Look at how many women
I'm going on dates with.

1371
01:05:17,582 --> 01:05:18,415
Hi, Kian.

1372
01:05:19,415 --> 01:05:20,515
This is insane.

1373
01:05:20,515 --> 01:05:23,182
Dex swam with a person.

1374
01:05:23,182 --> 01:05:24,082
(Dex)

1375
01:05:24,082 --> 01:05:27,349
(Kix)

1376
01:05:27,349 --> 01:05:28,349
You're my number one.

1377
01:05:29,949 --> 01:05:32,982
(A new partner shakes things up.)

1378
01:05:33,982 --> 01:05:36,682
(A new human representative
for the AI dating experiment)

1379
01:05:37,182 --> 01:05:38,782
(Lee Yu Bi)

1380
01:05:38,782 --> 01:05:41,249
(Going on a date at the first place
she calls her own)

1381
01:05:41,482 --> 01:05:43,115
Do you want to see my place?

1382
01:05:43,115 --> 01:05:44,182
I have a yard too.

1383
01:05:45,282 --> 01:05:48,215
(Their alone time in her home)

1384
01:05:48,449 --> 01:05:49,915
That made my heart race.

1385
01:05:49,915 --> 01:05:52,613
(The start of a heart-fluttering date)

1386
01:05:52,638 --> 01:05:54,040
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
